# AI majors take focuses in Hearts of Iron IV's own historical order (first available one wins);
# other countries, and anything not listed, pick at random.
# ---- FOCUS DESCRIPTIONS ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written for toi4 (2026-10-18) from the history of each country and what the focus does in the game - none of it
# is taken from Hearts of Iron IV. The focuses in FOCUS_TREES get their text from here when the game loads.
FOCUS_DESC = {
    # Generic (every other country)
    "ind_1":
        "Our workshops still run on habits from the last century. A national productivity drive - time studies, "
        "standard parts and a few modern machine tools bought abroad - will squeeze more out of every factory "
        "floor before we spend a single coin on new buildings.",
    "ind_2":
        "A modern economy moves on roads and rail as much as on machines. A corps of state construction engineers "
        "will survey the country, straighten the worst bottlenecks and put up a first new plant where the labour "
        "and the railway lines meet.",
    "ind_civ":
        "Prosperity is the best defence a small nation can buy. We will pour credit into consumer goods, power "
        "lines and roads, trusting that a richer country can always build weapons later - and that a content "
        "people will not look for strongmen.",
    "ind_mil":
        "The neighbours are arming, and waiting until they finish would be fatal. Arsenals, shell works and "
        "assembly halls come first now; the shops can stay half empty for a few more years if it means our "
        "soldiers have rifles in their hands when the time comes.",
    "army_1":
        "Our officers learned their trade in the trenches of the Great War, and many still think in those terms. "
        "A new staff college, fresh field manuals and a round of large manoeuvres will teach the army to move, "
        "strike and think faster.",
    "army_eq":
        "Too many of our reservists exist only on paper. Registering every able man, building depots in each "
        "district and giving the reserve regiments their own stocks of equipment will turn that list of names "
        "into an army we can actually call up.",
    "army_mob":
        "A small army cannot win a long war, so it must win a short one. A few motorised brigades and a first "
        "tank battalion, trained to strike deep into the enemy's rear, will give us a sword sharper than our size "
        "suggests.",
    "army_fp":
        "If we are attacked, every valley and river line must cost the invader dearly. Fortified belts along the "
        "border, a great reserve of infantry and plans to defend each town street by street will make any "
        "conquest too expensive to try.",
    "air_1":
        "Aircraft have changed war more than any weapon since gunpowder, and we cannot be left on the ground. A "
        "national aviation programme - flying schools, new airfields and licences to build modern designs - will "
        "give us an air arm worth the name.",
    "air_cas":
        "Our pilots should fly for the men in the mud. Training squadrons to work hand in hand with the infantry, "
        "hitting batteries, bridges and columns just ahead of an attack, will make the air force the army's most "
        "powerful artillery.",
    "air_strat":
        "Whoever rules the sky decides what happens beneath it. Fast fighters, a ring of observation posts and "
        "pilots trained to hunt the enemy's bombers will keep our cities and our soldiers safe from the air.",
    "pol_1":
        "Factions in parliament and squabbles between ministries waste the energy the country needs. A government "
        "of national effort, with a clear programme and a firm hand on the civil service, will let us act instead "
        "of debating.",
    "pol_col":
        "The old parties have failed, and the nation must stand as one body behind one will. Unions, youth and "
        "press will be gathered into state organisations and the economy bent to the national purpose - a path "
        "that alarms the democracies abroad.",
    "pol_mil":
        "A nation that wishes to survive must think like a soldier. Universal service, rifle clubs in every "
        "village and drill in the schools will give us the largest reserve our population allows, and a people "
        "ready to answer the call.",
    "pol_lib":
        "Our strength is the freedom of our citizens. A free press, honest elections and open markets will win "
        "the loyalty of the people and the sympathy of the great democracies, and an open economy will draw in "
        "trade and new ideas.",
    "pol_neu":
        "We will take no side in the quarrels of the great powers, but neutrality without guns is only an "
        "invitation. A modern frontier guard, new roads to bring reserves to the border and a declared readiness "
        "to fight will keep the armies of others away.",
    "naval_effort":
        "Our coast is long and our fleet is small and old. Expanding the naval yards and sending officers abroad "
        "to study modern ships will lay the foundations of a navy that can at least keep our own waters and "
        "harbours safe.",
    "flexible_navy":
        "We will never match the great fleets ship for ship, so we will not try. Light, fast vessels, submarines "
        "and raiders that strike at merchant traffic and vanish again will make any enemy pay for every cargo "
        "that crosses the sea.",
    "large_navy":
        "A real navy is built around heavy guns. A small squadron of capital ships and cruisers, kept together "
        "and well trained, will make even a great power think twice before it sails into our waters.",
    "submarine_effort":
        "The submarine is the poor nation's battleship. A new class of ocean-going boats with longer range, "
        "better torpedoes and quieter engines will let a few crews threaten the sea lanes of a far richer enemy.",
    "cruiser_effort":
        "Cruisers are the workhorses of any fleet: they scout, escort and fight wherever they are needed. A "
        "modern design, fast and well armed, will let our squadrons hold their own against anything short of a "
        "battleship.",
    "destroyer_effort":
        "Every convoy and every battle line needs a screen of destroyers. Improved designs with better guns, "
        "depth charges and listening gear will protect our merchant ships from submarines and our heavy ships "
        "from torpedo attack.",
    "capital_ships_effort":
        "Prestige at sea is still measured in heavy guns and flight decks. With our yards and crews now "
        "experienced enough, we can begin a modern battleship or carrier - a ship the whole nation will be proud "
        "to launch.",
    # German Reich
    "GER_develop_modern_maneuver_warfare":
        "The Reichswehr of the 1920s was kept small by Versailles, and its best minds spent those years thinking "
        "instead of drilling. Their ideas of speed, radio command and concentrated force must now become the "
        "doctrine of the whole army, before the old trench habits creep back in.",
    "GER_expanding_the_luftwaffe":
        "Officially Germany has had no air force since 1919; in truth pilots trained in secret at Lipetsk and in "
        "gliding clubs at home. Now that the Luftwaffe exists openly, it needs airfields, flight schools and "
        "modern aircraft in the numbers a great power requires.",
    "GER_strengthen_the_kriegsmarine":
        "The Anglo-German Naval Agreement of 1935 lets us build up to a third of the Royal Navy's tonnage. The "
        "shipyards at Kiel, Wilhelmshaven and Hamburg must be expanded at once if the fleet is ever to fill that "
        "allowance with real ships.",
    "GER_prioritize_economic_growth":
        "Hjalmar Schacht warns that rearmament on borrowed money cannot go on forever. Letting private industry "
        "grow first, with sound finances and exports to pay for raw materials, would build a broader economy - at "
        "the price of slower armament and a less patient party.",
    "GER_the_four_year_plan":
        "Hermann Göring will lead a new office with sweeping powers to make the economy ready for war within four "
        "years. Synthetic fuel, synthetic rubber and domestic ore will replace imports, and every ministry must "
        "bend to the demands of the plan.",
    "GER_remilitarize_the_rhineland":
        "Since Versailles the Rhineland has been a demilitarised zone that leaves our western industry open to "
        "any French advance. Sending a few battalions across the Rhine bridges is a gamble: if Paris answers with "
        "force we must retreat, but if the democracies only protest, we win back our own border without a shot.",
    "GER_fortify_the_vaterland":
        "A war on two fronts was our undoing in 1918. A line of bunkers, tank traps and gun positions along the "
        "western border will let a small force hold France at bay while the bulk of the army fights elsewhere.",
    "GER_aeronautical_research_institute":
        "Our aircraft industry is growing faster than the science behind it. A central institute with wind "
        "tunnels, test pilots and close ties to Junkers, Heinkel and Messerschmitt will turn ideas into "
        "production designs more quickly.",
    "GER_fallschirmjager":
        "The idea of soldiers dropping from the sky behind enemy lines still sounds like fantasy to many "
        "generals. A first parachute regiment, trained in secret, could seize bridges and fortresses before the "
        "defenders even know the war has begun.",
    "GER_form_the_jagdwaffe":
        "Bombers win headlines, but without fighters to protect them they are flying coffins. A dedicated fighter "
        "arm, built around the new Messerschmitt monoplane and pilots trained in aggressive tactics, will fight "
        "for command of the air over every battlefield.",
    "GER_plan_z":
        "Admiral Raeder dreams of a fleet able to meet the Royal Navy in open battle: battleships, carriers and "
        "heavy cruisers in great numbers by the mid-1940s. It will take years and enormous amounts of steel, but "
        "it would make Germany a true power at sea.",
    "GER_trade_interdiction":
        "Britain lives from imports. Rather than build a battle fleet we can never finish, we could aim straight "
        "at the merchant ships that feed her - with raiders, cruisers and above all submarines - and starve the "
        "island into peace.",
    "GER_currency_reforms":
        "Schacht's network of special bills and clearing agreements has kept the Reichsmark alive, but it cannot "
        "last. Restoring an honest currency would win back the trust of foreign traders and investors and free "
        "the economy to grow on firmer ground.",
    "GER_construct_the_reichsautobahn":
        "Thousands of workers are already building the first stretches of a national motorway network. Finishing "
        "it will tie the regions of the Reich together, put the unemployed to work and let troops and supplies "
        "cross the country in hours instead of days.",
    "GER_autarky_efforts":
        "A blockade starved Germany in the last war, and it must never happen again. Ersatz materials, new mines "
        "and chemical plants such as those at Leuna and Schkopau will make us less dependent on raw materials "
        "that an enemy fleet could cut off.",
    "GER_accelerate_the_rearmament_program":
        "The limits of Versailles are gone, but the army still has more plans than weapons. New arms factories "
        "must be built and the old ones run around the clock if the Wehrmacht is to be equipped before our "
        "neighbours wake up.",
    "GER_bribe_senior_officers":
        "Many generals of the old school look down on the party and its leader. Generous gifts, estates and "
        "promotions will soften their objections and make sure the army's leadership stays loyal when hard "
        "decisions are made.",
    "GER_heed_von_neuraths_concerns":
        "Foreign Minister von Neurath warns that moving too fast will unite Europe against us before we are "
        "ready. A slower, more careful course would buy time and keep the conservative elites of the foreign "
        "office and the army on our side.",
    "GER_reorganize_the_wehrmacht":
        "War Minister von Blomberg and the army chief von Fritsch question the pace of our plans. Taking supreme "
        "command away from them and placing it in the hands of the leader himself, through a new high command, "
        "will end the doubts at the top.",
    "GER_anti_comintern_pact":
        "Communism threatens every nation that values order. A common front against the Comintern, signed first "
        "with Japan and open to others, will give us partners abroad and present Germany to the world as Europe's "
        "bulwark against Moscow.",
    "GER_legion_condor":
        "The civil war in Spain is a chance to test our new weapons and tactics under real conditions. A "
        "volunteer air legion with tanks and anti-aircraft guns, sent to support Franco's nationalists, will "
        "bring home lessons no exercise could teach.",
    "GER_the_prussian_legacy":
        "Moltke, Schlieffen and the great general staff gave us a tradition of decisive manoeuvre and initiative "
        "at every level of command. We will build on that heritage: infantry and artillery led by officers who "
        "think quickly and act on their own.",
    "GER_adopt_new_panzer_doctrine":
        "Guderian argues that tanks should not crawl beside the infantry but drive in massed divisions, with "
        "their own artillery, engineers and radios, deep into the enemy's rear. It is a radical idea, and we will "
        "build our army around it.",
    "GER_dive_bombers":
        "A bomber that falls almost vertically onto its target can hit a bridge, a bunker or a ship with a "
        "precision no level bomber can match. The new Stuka will be the flying artillery of the Panzer divisions.",
    "GER_tactical_bombers":
        "Fast twin-engined bombers can strike airfields, railways and troop concentrations well behind the front, "
        "faster than enemy fighters can react. A strong force of them will support the army wherever it advances.",
    "GER_uralbomber_program":
        "General Wever believed that a future war would be decided by bombers able to reach the factories of the "
        "Urals and the north of Scotland. Four-engined heavy bombers are costly, but they would let us strike "
        "anywhere in Europe.",
    "GER_reorganize_the_luftwaffe":
        "The Luftwaffe grew so quickly that its command structure is a tangle of offices and rivalries. "
        "Reorganising it into air fleets, each responsible for a theatre of war, will make it ready to fight a "
        "real campaign.",
    "GER_experimental_rotorcrafts":
        "Focke and Flettner are building machines that rise straight into the air on spinning rotors. They are "
        "still curiosities, but research into them may one day give the navy and the army an aircraft that needs "
        "no runway.",
    "GER_develop_the_knickebein":
        "Bombing at night is blind work. A system of radio beams crossing over the target, which bombers can "
        "follow and listen for, would let our crews find a city in darkness and bad weather.",
    "GER_expand_kriegsmarinewerft":
        "The naval dockyard at Wilhelmshaven cannot build the great ships of Plan Z fast enough. New slipways, "
        "cranes and fitting-out basins will let us lay down battleships and our first aircraft carrier side by "
        "side.",
    "GER_re_establish_the_seekriegsleitung":
        "In the last war the navy had no single command to plan and lead its operations. A naval war staff in "
        "Berlin will draw up the strategy for every theatre and give the fleet a clear voice in the councils of "
        "war.",
    "GER_cruiser_warfare":
        "Fast heavy cruisers and armoured ships like the Deutschland can roam the oceans, sinking merchant ships "
        "far from home and drawing whole enemy squadrons away to hunt them. The more such raiders we build, the "
        "thinner the enemy fleet will be stretched.",
    "GER_wolfpack_tactics":
        "Commodore Dönitz believes U-boats should not hunt alone. Gathering several boats around a convoy, guided "
        "by radio from shore, and striking together at night would overwhelm the escorts and turn every crossing "
        "into a massacre of merchant ships.",
    "GER_lower_taxes":
        "High taxes still weigh on families and small businesses after years of crisis. Lowering them will give "
        "people money to spend, revive the shops and the workshops, and make the government more popular at home.",
    "GER_housing_developments":
        "Millions of Germans live in cramped tenements. A national programme of new housing estates will give "
        "workers decent homes near the factories and keep the building trades busy and loyal.",
    "GER_build_the_rur_dam":
        "A great dam in the Eifel will tame the floods of the Rur, store water for the Rhineland's cities and "
        "power new generating plants for industry.",
    "GER_kdf_wagen_factories":
        "The 'Strength through Joy' car was promised to every German family who saves for it. The vast new "
        "factory at Fallersleben can just as easily build vehicles and engines for the army when the need arises.",
    "GER_trade_deal_with_sweden":
        "Our blast furnaces depend on Swedish iron ore shipped through Narvik and Luleå. A long-term trade "
        "agreement, paid for with coal and machinery, will keep that ore flowing in peace and in war.",
    "GER_institute_price_controls":
        "Rearmament is pushing prices up faster than wages. A price commissioner with the power to freeze prices "
        "and ration scarce goods will keep inflation in check, though the shortages will not make us popular.",
    "GER_concentrated_armament_program":
        "Instead of spreading orders across hundreds of small firms, we will concentrate armament production in "
        "the largest and most efficient plants, with priority for steel, labour and power.",
    "GER_establish_production_targets":
        "Factories work best when they know exactly what is expected of them. Clear production quotas for every "
        "plant, checked each month by the ministry, will expose waste and reward the managers who deliver.",
    "GER_army_indoctrination":
        "Soldiers who fight for an idea fight harder than soldiers who only follow orders. Political officers and "
        "education programmes in every unit will make sure the army shares the convictions of the state.",
    "GER_autonomy_in_the_kriegsschulen":
        "The war academies have always trained officers to think for themselves. Leaving them free from party "
        "interference will keep the quality of our officer corps high, even if some instructors remain sceptical "
        "of the regime.",
    "GER_war_preparations":
        "Whatever course diplomacy takes, the army must be ready. Mobilisation plans, stockpiles of fuel and "
        "ammunition and detailed deployment schedules for every division will keep surprise from ever catching us "
        "unready.",
    "GER_anschluss":
        "Austria is German in language and culture, and many Austrians long to join the Reich. With pressure on "
        "Vienna and the threat of our army at the border, union can be achieved - the old dream of a Greater "
        "Germany.",
    "GER_uplift_the_rosenberg_office":
        "Alfred Rosenberg's office oversees the party's ideological schooling. Giving it more money and authority "
        "will spread the regime's ideas through schools, youth groups and the press, and bring more young men "
        "into the ranks.",
    "GER_molotov_ribbentrop_pact":
        "Stalin, too, has reasons to avoid a war with us - for now. A non-aggression treaty with Moscow, with "
        "secret agreements on spheres of influence in Eastern Europe, would let us deal with Poland and the West "
        "without fearing an attack from the east.",
    "GER_anti_soviet_pact":
        "Communism is our deadliest enemy, and no treaty with it is worth the paper. A firm alliance of the "
        "nations threatened by Moscow will prepare the ground for the great reckoning in the east.",
    "GER_befriend_china":
        "China has bought our weapons and hired our officers to train its armies. Strengthening these ties would "
        "win us a great market for our industry and a partner in Asia, even if it angers Tokyo.",
    "GER_befriend_japan":
        "Japan shares our hostility to communism and our wish to overturn the order of Versailles and Washington. "
        "A close alliance with Tokyo would give us a powerful partner on the far side of the Soviet Union.",
    "GER_improve_motorized_troops":
        "Tanks cannot win alone if the infantry follows on foot. Lorries, half-tracks and motorised supply "
        "columns will let whole divisions keep pace with the armour and hold the ground it takes.",
    "GER_lessons_of_the_great_war":
        "The last war was lost in the trenches, but it taught us infiltration tactics, storm troops and the value "
        "of surprise. A careful study of 1914 to 1918 will give our officers the lessons they need for the next "
        "one.",
    "GER_all_terrain_military_motorcycle":
        "Motorcycle troops can scout ahead of the army and carry messages along muddy tracks where no lorry can "
        "go. A rugged military motorcycle with a sidecar and a driven third wheel will give every division fast "
        "eyes and ears.",
    "GER_salvage_captured_equipment":
        "Every war leaves rifles, guns and vehicles on the battlefield. A dedicated service to collect, repair "
        "and reissue captured material will arm our second-line units without taking a single tonne of steel from "
        "the factories.",
    "GER_panzer_troops_school":
        "A new kind of army needs a new kind of soldier. A school for armoured warfare at Wünsdorf will train "
        "tank crews, radio operators and commanders who can lead fast units through the confusion of a "
        "breakthrough.",
    "GER_advanced_panzer_research":
        "Our first tanks were little more than training machines with machine guns. Heavier designs with real "
        "cannon, thicker armour and engines that do not break down after a day's march must be developed now, "
        "before we meet French and Soviet armour in battle.",
    "GER_torpedobomber":
        "A ship at sea is a small, moving target for a bomb, but a torpedo dropped low over the water strikes it "
        "below the waterline. Squadrons trained in this difficult art would give the Luftwaffe a real weapon "
        "against enemy fleets.",
    "GER_construct_aircraft_carriers":
        "Every modern navy is learning that aircraft can find and strike an enemy far beyond the range of any "
        "gun. Our first carrier, the Graf Zeppelin, has been laid down at Kiel; finishing her and her sister "
        "would give the fleet eyes and wings of its own.",
    "GER_grosskampfschiff_construction":
        "The heart of Plan Z is a squadron of new battleships larger and faster than anything now afloat. Laying "
        "down the first of them at once will commit the shipyards for years, but nothing else gives a navy such "
        "weight.",
    "GER_marinestosstrupp":
        "Sailors trained to storm a harbour, a coastal fort or an island from the sea are a weapon our army does "
        "not have. A naval assault force, practised in landings and close combat, will open the way for larger "
        "invasions.",
    "GER_atlantic_naval_bases":
        "Our ports on the North Sea are a long way from the Atlantic, and every ship must slip past Britain to "
        "reach it. Bases further west - and plans to use foreign harbours in wartime - would put the fleet within "
        "reach of the ocean trade routes.",
    "GER_panzerschiff_raiders":
        "The pocket battleships of the Deutschland class outgun any cruiser and can outrun any battleship. Sent "
        "out singly into the Atlantic and the Indian Ocean, they can tie down whole enemy squadrons and sink "
        "merchant ships far from any port.",
    "GER_u_boat_efforts":
        "The submarine nearly won the last war for us. A large fleet of modern ocean-going U-boats, built in "
        "series at many yards, will let us strike at Britain's lifelines from the first day of any war.",
    "GER_abolish_price_controls":
        "Controls and quotas strangle the initiative of our businessmen. Lifting them and letting prices find "
        "their level will bring goods back to the shops and confidence back to the markets.",
    "GER_industrial_expansion":
        "With taxes lower and workers housed, industry is ready to grow. Credit for new plants in the Ruhr, "
        "Saxony and Silesia will expand both civilian production and the armament works.",
    "GER_workers_rights":
        "Germany's workers built the economy and they deserve a fair share of its success. Paid holidays, safer "
        "factories and better canteens will make them more loyal and more productive.",
    "GER_expand_the_reichsautobahn_south":
        "A motorway through Bavaria towards the Alps and Austria will open the south to traffic and trade, and "
        "give the army a fast road towards our southern borders.",
    "GER_expand_the_reichsautobahn_east":
        "Extending the motorways eastward to Silesia and East Prussia will bind the eastern provinces to the "
        "heart of the Reich and speed the movement of goods and troops towards Poland.",
    "GER_establish_the_reichswerke":
        "Private steelmakers refuse to mine our poor domestic iron ore because it is not profitable. A great "
        "state-owned concern, the Reichswerke Hermann Göring at Salzgitter, will do it for them - at a cost the "
        "taxpayer must carry.",
    "GER_coal_liquefaction":
        "Germany has coal in abundance but almost no oil. The Bergius process turns coal into petrol, and new "
        "hydrogenation plants across the country will keep our tanks, planes and lorries moving even under "
        "blockade.",
    "GER_strafbataillon":
        "Soldiers who break discipline or fall foul of military courts need not sit in prison while others fight. "
        "Penal battalions will send them to the most dangerous tasks at the front - a harsh measure, but one that "
        "adds men to the line.",
    "GER_expand_the_truppenschulen":
        "The army is growing so quickly that it lacks trained sergeants and junior officers. More training "
        "grounds and schools for every branch will turn raw recruits into soldiers and give the new divisions "
        "their backbone.",
    "GER_reorganize_secret_services":
        "Military intelligence, the party's security service and the police all spy on the same people and seldom "
        "share what they learn. Clear responsibilities and a single chain of command will make our intelligence "
        "work far more effective.",
    "GER_befriend_czechoslovakia":
        "Czechoslovakia has a strong army, modern fortifications and the excellent Skoda works. A treaty of "
        "friendship that guarantees the rights of its German minority would make Prague a partner instead of a "
        "fortress on our flank.",
    "GER_demand_sudetenland":
        "Three million Germans live in the border regions of Czechoslovakia, and their leaders demand to join the "
        "Reich. If we press their claim hard enough, Britain and France may decide that it is not worth a war.",
    "GER_demonstration_of_military_achievements":
        "Great parades, air shows and newsreels of tanks rolling past cheering crowds will show the nation - and "
        "the world - how far the army has come since the days of Versailles.",
    "GER_reassert_eastern_claims":
        "The Polish Corridor cut East Prussia off from the rest of Germany, and Danzig was made a free city "
        "against its will. Raising these old grievances again will prepare our people for the struggle to come in "
        "the east.",
    "GER_the_triumphant_will":
        "The union with Austria has made the leader more popular than ever. A wave of rallies and celebrations "
        "across the Reich will turn that triumph into lasting authority at home.",
    "GER_support_a_coup_in_liechtenstein":
        "Liechtenstein is tiny, but it has its own local sympathisers of our movement. Quietly supporting them "
        "could bring the principality, and its small industry, into our orbit without a fight.",
    "GER_demand_slovenia":
        "The lands of the former Austrian Duchy of Carniola were once part of the same empire as Vienna. Now that "
        "Austria is ours, we can raise a claim to them against Yugoslavia.",
    "GER_expand_ss_recruitment":
        "Heinrich Himmler wants his armed SS formations to grow into a second army loyal only to the party. "
        "Opening their ranks to more volunteers will add men to our forces, though the generals resent the "
        "competition.",
    "GER_treaty_with_the_ussr":
        "The pact with Moscow can be more than a promise not to fight. A trade treaty that exchanges our machines "
        "for Soviet oil, grain and metals will feed our industry and blunt any British blockade.",
    "GER_support_finland":
        "Finland stands alone against the Soviet colossus. Sending it weapons, advisers and money will keep the "
        "Red Army busy on its northern flank and win us a grateful ally on the Baltic.",
    "GER_re_establish_german_control_over_qingdao":
        "Before 1914 Qingdao was a German port on the coast of China, with a naval base and the famous brewery. A "
        "friendly Chinese government might be persuaded to give us a foothold there again.",
    "GER_claim_old_colonies_in_the_east":
        "Our former possessions in the Pacific - New Guinea, Samoa and the islands - were taken from us in 1919. "
        "Raising our claim to them again will remind the world that Germany's place in the sun is not forgotten.",
    "GER_reclaim_former_african_colonies":
        "Togo, Cameroon, German South West Africa and German East Africa were handed to our enemies as mandates. "
        "Demanding their return is a matter of national honour, and a claim we can bring up at every conference.",
    "GER_japanese_naval_cooperation":
        "The Imperial Japanese Navy has built some of the most powerful carriers and battleships in the world. "
        "Exchanging designs, officers and experience with Tokyo would teach our fleet lessons that would take "
        "decades to learn alone.",
    "GER_artillery_bombardment":
        "Before the infantry attacks, the guns must break the enemy's lines. Short, violent bombardments directed "
        "by forward observers - the method perfected by Colonel Bruchmüller in 1918 - will shatter defences "
        "without warning the enemy hours in advance.",
    "GER_instill_auftragstaktik":
        "Our officers are told what to achieve, not how to achieve it. Spreading this mission-type command to "
        "every level of the army, down to the sergeant, will let our units seize chances that a rigid enemy would "
        "miss.",
    "GER_expand_kummersdorfs_capacity":
        "The proving grounds at Kummersdorf test every new gun, tank and vehicle before it goes into service. "
        "More ranges, workshops and engineers there will speed new designs from the drawing board into the hands "
        "of the troops.",
    "GER_combined_arms":
        "Tanks, motorised infantry, artillery, engineers and dive bombers are strongest when they fight as one "
        "team. Training them together, with radios linking them all, will make each Panzer division a "
        "self-contained striking force.",
    "GER_solve_the_logistical_bottlenecks":
        "An air force is only as good as its supply of fuel, spare parts and bombs. Mobile repair units, forward "
        "depots and a proper supply organisation will keep our squadrons flying when the front moves quickly.",
    "GER_defense_of_the_reich":
        "One day enemy bombers will try to strike at our cities and factories. A ring of radar stations, flak "
        "batteries and night fighters will make them pay dearly for every raid.",
    "GER_establish_carrier_groups":
        "A carrier alone is vulnerable, but a carrier screened by fast escorts and supported by its own torpedo "
        "bombers becomes the most dangerous ship on the ocean. Training our new carriers to fight in groups will "
        "make the most of them.",
    "GER_high_seas_fleet":
        "The Kaiser's High Seas Fleet once challenged Britannia for command of the North Sea. Its successor will "
        "be a balanced fleet of battleships, carriers and cruisers able to fight its way out into the Atlantic.",
    "GER_atlantic_naval_dominance":
        "With bases on the Atlantic coast and a fleet trained to use them, we can contest the ocean itself. "
        "Wherever our ships and U-boats gather, enemy shipping will have to turn back or pay a terrible price.",
    "GER_unrestricted_convoy_raiding":
        "In the last war, restraint at sea cost us the chance of victory. This time every ship sailing to an "
        "enemy port, whatever its flag, will be treated as a target.",
    "GER_increased_trade":
        "With price controls gone, our goods are competitive again. New trade agreements with the Balkans, "
        "Scandinavia and South America will bring in raw materials and foreign currency.",
    "GER_invest_in_vereinigte_stahlwerke":
        "The United Steelworks of the Ruhr is the largest steel concern in Europe. State credit for new furnaces "
        "and rolling mills there will lift the output of both our civilian industry and the armament works.",
    "GER_agricultural_reforms":
        "Germany cannot feed itself in a long war. Better fertilisers, machines for the farms and new land "
        "drained and ploughed will free workers for the factories and make us less dependent on imported food.",
    "GER_develop_heraeus_facilities":
        "The Heraeus works at Hanau are leaders in precious metals and precision instruments. Expanding their "
        "laboratories will give our scientists better tools for every branch of military research.",
    "GER_seize_foreign_industries":
        "Foreign-owned firms on German soil answer to boards abroad. Placing them under German administration "
        "brings their factories into our plans - though such methods frighten foreign investors.",
    "GER_subsidize_hoesch_benzin":
        "The Hoesch-Benzin plant in Dortmund turns Ruhr coal into fuel. State subsidies will let it grow and "
        "prove that synthetic petrol can be produced on a truly national scale.",
    "GER_establish_buna_werke":
        "Without rubber there are no tyres, no seals and no hoses for the army's vehicles. The Buna works at "
        "Schkopau will make synthetic rubber from coal and lime, and free us from imports from overseas "
        "plantations.",
    "GER_zentrale_planung":
        "Every ministry, the services and the four-year plan office all fight over the same steel and labour. A "
        "central planning board with the final word on allocations will end the chaos, even if it slows things "
        "down while it settles in.",
    "GER_innovative_warfare":
        "War is changing faster than any manual can be written. Encouraging officers to experiment with new "
        "tactics and to report honestly on what fails will keep the army ahead of its enemies.",
    "GER_prepare_for_the_next_blockade_ww":
        "Britain will blockade us again the moment war begins. Stockpiles of oil, rubber and metals, a merchant "
        "fleet ready to sail on short notice and plans for rationing will let the nation endure what broke it in "
        "1918.",
    "GER_first_vienna_award":
        "Hungary has old claims on southern Slovakia. By arbitrating between Budapest and Prague in our favour, "
        "we can reward a friend and weaken what is left of Czechoslovakia at the same time.",
    "GER_an_invincible_army":
        "Victory after victory has convinced the nation that its army cannot be beaten. Thousands of young men "
        "are volunteering to join it, and the propaganda ministry will make sure that the legend keeps growing.",
    "GER_first_ljubljana_award":
        "With Slovenia in our hands, its neighbours want their share of the old border lands. Settling their "
        "claims in Ljubljana under our arbitration will bind them more tightly to Berlin.",
    "GER_alliance_with_the_ussr":
        "The non-aggression pact has worked better than either side expected. Turning it into a true alliance, "
        "with Moscow and Berlin dividing their spheres across Europe and Asia, would leave Britain without a "
        "single friend on the continent.",
    "GER_war_with_the_ussr":
        "The pact with Stalin was only ever a pause. The vast farmland, oil and resources of the Soviet Union are "
        "the real prize, and the Red Army, weakened by its own purges, may never be easier to defeat than now.",
    "GER_ally_chiang_kai_shek":
        "Chiang Kai-shek's China has been trained by our officers and armed with our weapons for years. A formal "
        "alliance would give us a partner of four hundred million people in Asia, though it would turn Japan "
        "against us for good.",
    "GER_mittelafrika":
        "Before 1914 our planners imagined a German Central Africa stretching from coast to coast. If our old "
        "colonies return, they could form the core of such an empire and supply the Reich with tropical raw "
        "materials and colonial troops.",
    "GER_negotiate_old_colonies_in_the_east":
        "Japan took our Pacific islands in 1914 and holds them as a League mandate. As allies, we may be able to "
        "agree on their future in a way that suits both Tokyo and Berlin.",
    "GER_stormtroopers":
        "In 1918 small groups of storm troops with grenades, light machine guns and flamethrowers slipped through "
        "the British lines and nearly broke them. Training every infantry division in these assault tactics will "
        "give our attacks the same cutting edge.",
    "GER_establish_the_afrikakorps":
        "Italy's armies in Libya may one day need help against the British in Egypt. Preparing an expeditionary "
        "corps for desert warfare - with tropical equipment, water supply and trained mechanics - would let us "
        "send aid quickly when the call comes.",
    "GER_panzergrenadier":
        "Infantry that rides into battle in armoured half-tracks can keep up with the tanks and fight alongside "
        "them. Panzergrenadier regiments will hold the ground the panzers win and clear the obstacles that stop "
        "them.",
    "GER_establish_the_skijager":
        "Wars in the north and the east will be fought in deep snow and bitter cold. Ski troops trained in winter "
        "warfare, with sledges and white camouflage, can move where other units are stuck.",
    "GER_rocketry_innovations":
        "At Peenemünde, Wernher von Braun and his team are building rockets that could one day carry a warhead "
        "hundreds of kilometres. Funding their work now may give us a weapon no enemy can stop.",
    "GER_construct_the_kammhuber_line":
        "General Kammhuber proposes a belt of radar stations, searchlights and night fighter zones across the "
        "approaches to the Reich. Each enemy bomber that crosses it would be tracked and handed to a fighter "
        "waiting in the dark.",
    "GER_establish_night_fighter_squadrons":
        "Enemy bombers will come at night, when our day fighters are almost blind. Squadrons equipped with "
        "twin-engined fighters and airborne radar, flown by crews trained for the dark, will hunt them over our "
        "cities.",
    "GER_seeherrschaft":
        "With a powerful surface fleet and unrestricted war against enemy trade, we can do what the Kaiser's navy "
        "never could: win command of the sea for Germany.",
    "GER_wirtschaftswunder":
        "Sound money, open trade and investment have put the economy on a path of rapid growth. If we keep the "
        "course, the coming years may bring an economic miracle that makes Germany the richest nation in Europe.",
    "GER_urbanization":
        "As farms modernise, millions of rural workers are moving to the cities. Planning new districts, "
        "transport and services for them will turn that migration into a source of labour for industry.",
    "GER_autarky_achieved":
        "Synthetic fuel, synthetic rubber, domestic ore and the industries of the lands we have absorbed mean "
        "that Germany can at last stand on its own. No blockade can starve us again.",
    "GER_armament_rationalization":
        "Too many types of weapons and vehicles are built in too many small batches. Cutting the number of "
        "designs, standardising parts and building in long series will raise output without a single new factory.",
    "GER_create_rustungsstab":
        "An armament staff with authority over industry, labour and raw materials will drive production forward "
        "with the urgency of a military command, overruling every ministry that stands in the way.",
    "GER_subversive_infiltrators":
        "Agents placed in neighbouring countries - among discontented minorities, sympathetic parties and the "
        "press - can weaken their governments from inside and prepare the ground for our demands.",
    "GER_integrate_czechoslovakia":
        "Our friendship with Prague has drawn Czechoslovakia ever closer into our orbit. The final step is to "
        "bring Bohemia and Moravia fully into the Reich, along with their skilled workers and the Skoda works.",
    "GER_fate_of_czechoslovakia":
        "Weakened by the loss of the Sudetenland and torn by quarrels between Czechs and Slovaks, the "
        "Czechoslovak state is close to falling apart. Our troops can occupy Bohemia and Moravia before anyone "
        "else can react.",
    "GER_the_supreme_leader":
        "With the army's victories behind him, the leader's authority is beyond question. Every office of party "
        "and state now answers to him alone.",
    "GER_expand_claims_in_baltic":
        "Memel was taken from East Prussia after the war, and German communities have lived along the Baltic "
        "coast for centuries. Pressing claims on those lands will extend our reach along the sea.",
    "GER_influence_the_baltics":
        "Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania fear the Soviet Union more than they fear us. Trade agreements and quiet "
        "guarantees can bring them into our sphere without a single soldier crossing their borders.",
    "GER_fate_of_yugoslavia":
        "Yugoslavia is a fragile union of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes held together by Belgrade. Encouraging "
        "Croatian separatists and pressing our claims could break it apart and open the Balkans to us.",
    "GER_puppet_turkey":
        "With Moscow's support, we can push Ankara into an alliance it cannot refuse. A friendly Turkey controls "
        "the straits between the Black Sea and the Mediterranean and opens the road to the Middle East.",
    "GER_befriend_turkey":
        "Turkey fought beside us in the Great War and has every reason to fear Russia. Courting Ankara with "
        "credits and arms would gain us a partner on the southern flank of the Soviet Union.",
    "GER_create_asian_reichskommissariat":
        "Should territories in Asia fall under our control, they will need German administrators to govern them. "
        "Planning these occupation authorities now, with our Chinese or Japanese partners, prepares us for an "
        "empire on the far side of the world.",
    "GER_south_east_asian_natural_wealth":
        "The rubber of Malaya, the tin of the Dutch Indies and the oil of Borneo are the riches our industry "
        "lacks most. With partners in Asia, we can secure a share of that wealth for the Reich.",
    "GER_sentinels_of_the_pacific":
        "Our navy and Japan's can watch over the Pacific together. Shared bases, joint exercises and coordinated "
        "plans will let a small German presence in the region punch far above its weight.",
    "GER_nationalize_ford_factories":
        "Ford's plant in Cologne builds lorries that our army needs in large numbers. Placing the American-owned "
        "factory under German control will turn its production entirely towards the Wehrmacht.",
    "GER_improve_the_logistics_system":
        "Mechanised armies devour fuel, ammunition and spare parts. More lorries, field workshops and well-run "
        "railheads will keep supplies moving behind the front when the panzers advance fast and far.",
    "GER_defend_the_vaterland":
        "Should the enemy ever reach our borders, every town and river must be defended. Training the army in "
        "stubborn defence and counter-attack will make the homeland a fortress.",
    "GER_kriegslokomotiven":
        "The railways are the arteries of the war effort, and they wear out fast in a long campaign. A simple "
        "wartime locomotive, built quickly in great numbers, will keep the trains running from the Channel to the "
        "Russian steppe.",
    "GER_aerodynamic_research_institute":
        "Jet engines and swept wings may soon make the propeller obsolete. A new institute for high-speed "
        "aerodynamics, with wind tunnels able to test near the speed of sound, will keep our aircraft ahead of "
        "any enemy.",
    "GER_mass_production":
        "The growing economy can now turn out goods in quantities no one dreamed of a few years ago. The same "
        "methods of assembly-line production can be applied to weapons, building them by the thousand.",
    "GER_build_defense_industry":
        "A prosperous country with no arms industry is a prize waiting for a thief. Using our new wealth to build "
        "modern armament plants will make sure that prosperity can be defended.",
    "GER_totaler_krieg":
        "The war will not be won by half measures. Closing luxury shops, calling up every available worker and "
        "putting the whole nation's life at the service of the front will show our enemies that Germany is ready "
        "to fight to the end.",
    "GER_integrate_czech_manufacturers":
        "The Skoda and CKD works produce some of the finest guns and tanks in Europe. Bringing them into our "
        "armament programme adds whole divisions' worth of equipment every year.",
    "GER_danzig_for_slovakia":
        "Poland has long wanted a say in the future of Slovakia. Offering Warsaw influence there in return for "
        "Danzig and a road across the Corridor could settle the eastern question without a war.",
    "GER_danzig_or_war":
        "Danzig is a German city, and the Corridor that separates East Prussia from the Reich is an open wound. "
        "If Poland will not return them peacefully, the army must be ready to take them back by force.",
    "GER_second_ljubljana_award":
        "Yugoslavia's neighbours still have claims of their own. A second settlement under our arbitration can "
        "redraw the borders of the Balkans and bind those states to us even more closely.",
    "GER_war_with_greece":
        "Greece stands in the way of our influence over the Balkans and leans towards Britain. If it will not "
        "bend, the army must go through the mountains of Macedonia to Athens.",
    "GER_influence_the_middle_east":
        "Arab nationalists in Iraq, Syria and Palestine resent British and French rule. Supporting them with "
        "money, weapons and propaganda could threaten the oil and the routes that sustain the British Empire.",
    "GER_the_final_blow_to_communism":
        "With the Soviet Union at war with us, there can be no compromise. Every resource of the Reich must now "
        "go towards breaking the Red Army before Russia's endless reserves can be mobilised.",
    "GER_the_proud_eagle_and_the_resurgent_dragon":
        "Germany and China, two old nations reborn, can stand together as equals. A grand partnership of the "
        "German eagle and the Chinese dragon would shape the future of both Europe and Asia.",
    "GER_blitzkrieg_across_the_pacific":
        "The lessons of mobile warfare learned in Europe can be applied in Asia too. Training our forces and "
        "partners in fast amphibious and mechanised operations will let them seize the islands and coasts of the "
        "Pacific before the enemy can respond.",
    "GER_uranverein":
        "Our physicists have discovered that the uranium atom can be split, releasing enormous energy. A national "
        "research group to study this fission may one day give us an unlimited source of power - or a weapon of "
        "terrible strength.",
    "GER_amerikabomber":
        "Even America may not be safe forever. A bomber with the range to fly from Europe to New York and back "
        "would force the United States to keep its fighters and guns at home.",
    "GER_war_production":
        "With the economy in full swing, it is time to turn more of its strength into weapons. New plants and "
        "expanded shifts will give the army, navy and air force the equipment for a long war.",
    "GER_befriend_poland":
        "With Danzig settled, Warsaw no longer has a reason to fear us. A friendly Poland, perhaps a partner "
        "against the Soviet Union, would secure our eastern frontier.",
    "GER_subjugate_romanian_economy":
        "The oil fields of Ploiești are the richest in Europe outside Russia. Trade agreements that tie Romania's "
        "economy to ours will give the Reich the fuel it needs and make Bucharest depend on Berlin.",
    "GER_fate_of_greece":
        "Greece has refused every settlement we offered. With the Balkans now in our hands, there is nothing left "
        "to stop us from forcing the issue.",
    "GER_fuhrerprinzip":
        "In the new Germany, authority flows from the top and responsibility rises from below. Applying the "
        "leader principle to every ministry, company and association will cut through committees and endless "
        "debate.",
    "GER_influence_the_benelux":
        "Belgium, the Netherlands and Luxembourg would rather stay out of any war. Persuading them to keep their "
        "neutrality - and to keep the British and French off their soil - would protect our western flank.",
    "GER_around_maginot":
        "The Maginot Line is too strong to attack head-on, but it ends at the Belgian border. Striking through "
        "the Low Countries - perhaps even through the wooded hills of the Ardennes - would outflank France's "
        "defences entirely.",
    "GER_operation_weserubung":
        "Swedish iron ore reaches us through the Norwegian port of Narvik, and the Royal Navy would love to cut "
        "that route. Seizing Denmark and Norway in a single swift operation would secure the ore and give our "
        "fleet bases on the open Atlantic.",
    "GER_utilize_the_nordliche_gesellschaft":
        "The Nordic Society promotes cultural ties between Germany and the Scandinavian and Baltic peoples. Using "
        "its network of friends and sympathisers, we can win influence across the north without firing a shot.",
    "GER_ascension_of_todt":
        "Fritz Todt built the motorways and the West Wall on time and on budget. Raising him to the highest rank "
        "of the party will give his engineering talent authority over construction across the Reich.",
    "GER_ascension_of_speer":
        "Albert Speer, the young architect, has impressed the leader with his drive and his gift for "
        "organisation. Giving him real power over production may get more out of our industry than any general "
        "could.",
    "GER_ascension_of_goring":
        "Hermann Göring already commands the Luftwaffe and the Four-Year Plan. Confirming him as the second man "
        "of the Reich will give the economy a single, if erratic, master.",
    "GER_ascension_of_himmler":
        "Heinrich Himmler controls the police and the SS, and both are growing fast. Placing him at the top of "
        "the party hierarchy will bring their formations - and their recruits - fully into the service of the "
        "state.",
    "GER_ascension_of_goebbels":
        "Joseph Goebbels controls the press, the radio and the cinema. With his authority raised, every newspaper "
        "and newsreel will speak with one voice to keep the nation behind the war.",
    "GER_party_chancellor_hess":
        "Rudolf Hess, the deputy leader, is loyal but increasingly withdrawn. Keeping him at the head of the "
        "party chancellery preserves the old guard and a predictable chain of command.",
    "GER_party_chancellor_bormann":
        "Martin Bormann works quietly behind the scenes, controlling access to the leader and the party's "
        "finances. Giving him the party chancellery will make him one of the most powerful men in the Reich.",
    "GER_form_rome_berlin_axis":
        "Mussolini's Italy and our Germany share the same enemies and the same ambitions. A formal alliance - an "
        "axis around which Europe will turn - will unite the two revolutions and make both stronger.",
    "GER_invade_italy":
        "Mussolini has proved an unreliable partner, and his armies are weaker than his speeches. Seizing the "
        "Alpine passes and northern Italy would give us full control of southern Europe.",
    "GER_war_with_france":
        "France has been our enemy for centuries and twice humbled us. With our eastern frontier secure, the time "
        "has come to settle the account in the west.",
    "GER_demands_to_sweden":
        "Sweden's ore keeps our blast furnaces running, and with Norway in our hands it has nowhere else to turn. "
        "We can demand transit rights and guaranteed deliveries - and Stockholm will have little choice but to "
        "agree.",
    "GER_secure_finland":
        "Finland has fought the Soviet Union once already and will fight again. Treaties, weapons and German "
        "troops in Lapland will make it a firm partner on the northern flank.",
    "GER_form_organization_todt":
        "A single state construction agency, employing hundreds of thousands of workers, can build "
        "fortifications, roads and factories wherever the war requires them.",
    "GER_employ_philipp_holzmann":
        "Philipp Holzmann is one of the largest construction firms in Europe, with engineers who have built "
        "railways from Anatolia to South America. Contracting it for national projects will raise new industry "
        "quickly.",
    "GER_prioritize_the_four_year_plan":
        "Göring's office will be given first claim on raw materials, labour and investment. Every other ministry "
        "must give way to the plan.",
    "GER_expand_gestapo":
        "The secret state police watches over the home front for spies, saboteurs and opponents of the regime. "
        "Giving it more agents and wider powers will keep the Reich quiet behind the lines - through fear.",
    "GER_expand_ss_security_duties":
        "Behind the front, the SS will take over security in occupied lands. This adds armed men to our forces "
        "but costs political capital and, in the long run, the trust of the populations we rule.",
    "GER_ministry_of_public_enlightenment":
        "Goebbels' ministry will receive more money for radio sets, films and posters. A people that hears only "
        "one story will be easier to keep behind the war effort.",
    "GER_optimize_reich_labour_service":
        "Every young German serves six months in the Reich Labour Service, draining marshes and building roads. "
        "Organising that service better will turn more of its labour towards the economy's real needs.",
    "GER_alliance_with_spain":
        "General Franco owes his victory in the civil war partly to our help. An alliance with Madrid would open "
        "the road to Gibraltar and close the western Mediterranean to the British.",
    "GER_operation_felix":
        "If Franco will not join us willingly, we can take Gibraltar ourselves. A rapid strike through Spain to "
        "seize the Rock would lock the Royal Navy out of the Mediterranean.",
    "GER_operation_sea_lion":
        "As long as Britain stands, the war cannot be won. An invasion across the Channel needs barges, landing "
        "craft and air superiority over southern England - preparations that must begin now.",
    "GER_operation_tannenbaum":
        "Switzerland's mountains and banks have sheltered our enemies for too long. Surrounded by Axis territory, "
        "it could be conquered in a short campaign if we are prepared to fight in the Alps.",
    "GER_the_swiss_gold":
        "Neutral Switzerland can be more useful as a banker than as a battlefield. Swiss francs and Swiss banks "
        "will let us buy the raw materials that we cannot get any other way.",
    "GER_autonomous_organization_todt":
        "If Organisation Todt answers only to the leader, it can cut through red tape and build without "
        "interference - though the ministries and the party will resent losing control.",
    "GER_plenipotentiary_of_armaments":
        "A single minister with full authority over armaments production can coordinate industry like a great "
        "machine and raise output far beyond the current level.",
    "GER_plenipotentiary_of_the_four_year_plan":
        "Making the head of the Four-Year Plan the economy's undisputed master will tie every factory, mine and "
        "farm to a single will.",
    "GER_absorb_the_abwehr":
        "Admiral Canaris's military intelligence service is suspected of disloyalty. Bringing it under the "
        "control of the SS security service would give us one intelligence apparatus, loyal to the regime.",
    "GER_strengthen_the_waffen_ss":
        "The armed SS divisions are growing into a separate army with its own equipment and recruits. Giving them "
        "priority will produce elite formations - at the expense of the regular Wehrmacht.",
    "GER_fund_the_film_department":
        "Cinemas are full every night, and films reach people that speeches never will. Funding grand historical "
        "epics and newsreels from the front will keep the nation's spirits high.",
    "GER_rally_the_industrialists":
        "Krupp, Thyssen and the other great industrial families funded the movement in its early days. Bringing "
        "them together again behind the regime's goals will secure their factories and their loyalty.",
    "GER_glorify_party_rallies":
        "The rallies at Nuremberg are designed to overwhelm: searchlights, banners and hundreds of thousands "
        "marching in step. Making them grander still will show the nation that the movement is unstoppable.",
    "GER_alliance_with_portugal":
        "Portugal's Salazar is no friend of the democracies, and his country guards the Atlantic coast of Iberia. "
        "Bringing Lisbon into our camp would close the last friendly port in the region to the British.",
    "GER_operation_isabella":
        "If Portugal remains Britain's oldest ally, its ports and the Azores could become British bases. A plan "
        "to occupy them first would deny the enemy a foothold on the Iberian Atlantic coast.",
    "GER_operation_green":
        "Ireland is neutral, but its coast lies across Britain's western approaches. Landing there would let us "
        "strike at Britain from behind and cut its shipping routes to America.",
    "GER_reintegrate_luxemburg_and_alsace_lorraine":
        "Alsace, Lorraine and Luxembourg were German before 1918, and many there still speak German dialects. "
        "With France defeated, they can be brought back into the Reich and their men called to its service.",
    "GER_wunderwaffe":
        "Rockets, jet aircraft and other new weapons may yet change the course of the war. Pouring resources into "
        "these wonder weapons is a gamble, but one that could give us a decisive edge.",
    "GER_integration_of_puppet_economies":
        "The industries of the occupied and allied countries can be organised into one great European economy "
        "under German direction, supplying the Reich with everything it needs.",
    "GER_hegemony_of_the_ss":
        "The SS now controls the police, security and its own armed divisions. Giving it the final word over "
        "internal affairs will make it the true power behind the state.",
    "GER_propaganda_master":
        "With radio, film and press entirely under our control, we can make the people believe almost anything. "
        "Even defeats can be turned into heroic stands.",
    "GER_total_control_over_domestic_affairs":
        "With the party chancellery in control of every office, the leader's will is carried out without delay or "
        "debate across the whole Reich.",
    "GER_crossing_the_atlantic":
        "With Britain defeated, the next challenge lies across the ocean. Long-range transports, landing craft "
        "and naval infantry must be prepared for operations in the New World.",
    "GER_a_strong_successor":
        "The leader will not live forever, and a state built around one man risks chaos when he is gone. Naming a "
        "strong successor now will keep the Reich stable whatever happens.",
    "GER_loyalty_to_the_fuhrer":
        "Talk of successors only encourages plots. The whole nation and every officer of the army must swear "
        "their loyalty to the leader alone.",
    "GER_challenge_the_monroe_doctrine":
        "For over a century the United States has claimed the right to exclude European powers from the Americas. "
        "It is time to challenge that claim, starting with friendly governments in South America.",
    "GER_shatter_usas_hegemony":
        "The United States dominates the western hemisphere through money and the threat of its fleet. Breaking "
        "that hold will open the Americas to our influence and our trade.",
    "GER_establish_protectorates_in_america":
        "Governments in South and Central America that lean towards us can be brought under our protection, "
        "giving the Reich a foothold on the far side of the Atlantic.",
    # Soviet Union
    "SOV_infrastructure_effort_nsb":
        "Our country is vast and its roads are mud for half the year. New railway lines, paved highways and "
        "electricity for the countryside will tie the republics together and carry the products of the five-year "
        "plans to where they are needed.",
    "SOV_heavy_industry":
        "Steel, coal and machines are the foundation of socialism and of national defence. Magnitogorsk and the "
        "other giants of the first plans must be followed by new mills and works, built faster than the "
        "capitalists believe possible.",
    "SOV_transpolar_flights":
        "Chkalov's flight over the North Pole to America has shown the world what Soviet aviation can do. More "
        "record flights will inspire the young, impress foreign observers and push our designers to build ever "
        "better aircraft.",
    "SOV_expand_the_red_fleet":
        "The Red Fleet is a shadow of the Tsar's navy, with old battleships and few modern vessels. A programme "
        "of new destroyers and cruisers for the Baltic, the Black Sea, the North and the Pacific will begin to "
        "change that.",
    "SOV_found_the_pcdi":
        "Defence production is scattered across many commissariats that compete for the same resources. A "
        "People's Commissariat of the Defence Industry will take control of all armament plants and run them "
        "according to one plan.",
    "SOV_strengthen_the_mobilization_plan":
        "If war comes, millions of reservists must reach their units within days. Updating the mobilisation "
        "registers, the depots and the railway timetables will make sure the Red Army can grow quickly to its "
        "full wartime size.",
    "SOV_the_path_of_marxism_leninism":
        "The revolution of 1917 gave power to the workers and peasants; now the Party must guide the country "
        "towards socialism. Strict loyalty to the teachings of Marx, Engels and Lenin, as interpreted by Comrade "
        "Stalin, will show the way.",
    "SOV_finish_the_five_year_plan":
        "The Second Five-Year Plan must be completed on time, whatever the effort. Its new factories, mines and "
        "power stations will lift the output of the whole economy and prove the superiority of planning over the "
        "market.",
    "SOV_expand_the_aircraft_industry":
        "The air force of the future will need thousands of machines. New aircraft and engine plants in Moscow, "
        "Kazan, Gorky and beyond will let our designers' best work be built in the numbers a great war demands.",
    "SOV_foster_flying_clubs":
        "Through Osoaviakhim, the society for defence and aviation, young workers learn to fly and parachute in "
        "their free time. Spreading these clubs to every city will give the air force a vast pool of trained "
        "pilots.",
    "SOV_reinforce_western_naval_bases":
        "Leningrad and Kronstadt guard the approaches to our second city, but the Gulf of Finland is narrow and "
        "easy to mine. Stronger bases and new yards on the Baltic will let the fleet defend the capital of the "
        "revolution.",
    "SOV_reinforce_northern_naval_bases":
        "Murmansk stays free of ice all year and opens directly onto the Atlantic. Building it into a proper "
        "naval base will give the fleet a door to the ocean that no enemy can easily close.",
    "SOV_reinforce_southern_naval_bases":
        "Sevastopol and the other Black Sea ports protect the Crimea and the oil of the Caucasus. Expanding them "
        "will secure our southern coast and give the Black Sea Fleet room to grow.",
    "SOV_reinforce_eastern_naval_bases":
        "Vladivostok sits within easy reach of Japan's navy. Stronger defences and a better-supplied Pacific "
        "Fleet will make Tokyo think twice about any adventure against the Soviet Far East.",
    "SOV_pc_of_mechanical_engineering":
        "A separate commissariat for mechanical engineering will organise the production of tanks, tractors and "
        "machine tools. Clear leadership and priority supplies will make the factories of Kharkov and Leningrad "
        "work as one.",
    "SOV_military_engineering_university":
        "Modern war needs officers who understand engines, bridges and fortifications. A military engineering "
        "academy will train the specialists the army needs to build, maintain and destroy.",
    "SOV_restore_cossack_units":
        "The Cossacks were once the Tsar's most feared horsemen, and were disbanded after the civil war. Allowing "
        "them to serve again in their own units would add tough, mobile cavalry to the Red Army and win back "
        "their loyalty.",
    "SOV_cohesion_first":
        "A modern army must be a single body, without special privileges for any people or group. Mixing recruits "
        "from every republic into the same units, under the same discipline, will build a truly Soviet army.",
    "SOV_the_centre":
        "Power must flow from one place: the Central Committee of the Party and the leader who stands at its "
        "head. Every commissariat, every regional committee and every factory director must follow the line set "
        "in Moscow.",
    "SOV_addressing_internal_affairs":
        "Comrade Stalin warns that enemies of the people hide inside the Party, the army and the economy. A great "
        "campaign to root them out will make the state secure - though many loyal citizens will also be swept "
        "away in the process.",
    "SOV_the_comintern":
        "The Communist International links the workers' parties of the whole world to Moscow. Giving it more "
        "money and clearer instructions will make it a powerful tool of Soviet foreign policy.",
    "SOV_improve_railway_network":
        "The railways carry almost everything the Soviet economy produces, and they are overloaded. Doubling the "
        "main lines, building new ones to the Urals and Siberia and modernising the rolling stock will free "
        "industry from its bottlenecks.",
    "SOV_third_five_year_plan":
        "The Third Five-Year Plan will put greater weight on chemicals, defence industry and the development of "
        "the east. Its targets are ambitious, and every worker must give their best to meet them.",
    "SOV_national_specialists":
        "Soviet schools and institutes are now producing engineers and scientists in large numbers. Relying on "
        "our own specialists will keep foreign influence out of our factories and prove that socialism can stand "
        "on its own feet.",
    "SOV_foreign_experts":
        "American and German engineers helped build our first great factories. Hiring more foreign specialists, "
        "and buying their licences and machines, will bring the latest technology to Soviet industry faster.",
    "SOV_modernize_aircraft_facilities":
        "Many aircraft factories still build by hand what the capitalists build on assembly lines. Modern machine "
        "tools, jigs and production methods will raise both the quality and the quantity of our planes.",
    "SOV_expand_aviation_institutes":
        "The Central Aero-Hydrodynamic Institute and the design bureaus of Tupolev, Polikarpov and Ilyushin need "
        "more engineers and laboratories. Expanding them will give the air force better aircraft for the coming "
        "war.",
    "SOV_women_in_aviation":
        "Soviet women already fly records across the country, and many more train in the flying clubs. Opening "
        "military aviation to them will double the pool of pilots and show that socialism has freed women to "
        "serve the motherland.",
    "SOV_expand_shipbuilding_plants":
        "New shipyards at Molotovsk in the north and on the Amur in the Far East, along with expanded yards in "
        "Leningrad and Nikolaev, will let us build a fleet worthy of a great power.",
    "SOV_pc_of_the_ussr_navy":
        "The navy has long been treated as an appendage of the army. A separate People's Commissariat for the "
        "Navy will give it its own leadership, budget and shipbuilding programme.",
    "SOV_superior_war_machines":
        "Soviet engineers can design tanks that surpass anything in the West. Giving the design bureaus the "
        "freedom and resources to experiment will produce machines with better guns, thicker armour and wider "
        "tracks.",
    "SOV_the_means_to_wage_war":
        "Designs are useless without factories to build them. Converting tractor plants, expanding gun works and "
        "training thousands of new workers will give the Red Army the weapons it needs in the numbers it needs.",
    "SOV_move_industry_to_the_urals":
        "Our western industry lies within reach of any invader from Europe. Building new plants beyond the Volga "
        "and preparing to move whole factories east by rail will keep the economy alive even if the west is lost.",
    "SOV_the_molotov_line":
        "As the border moves west, a new line of fortifications must protect it. Concrete bunkers along the new "
        "frontier will stop an enemy at the very edge of Soviet territory.",
    "SOV_improve_the_stalin_line":
        "The Stalin Line of fortified districts along the old western border can be strengthened instead. "
        "Modernising its bunkers and adding artillery will give the army a strong defence line deeper inside the "
        "country.",
    "SOV_far_east_fortification":
        "Japan's army in Manchuria faces our long border along the Amur and the Ussuri. Fortified regions, "
        "airfields and supply bases in the Far East will make any Japanese attack costly.",
    "SOV_rehabilitated_military":
        "Many experienced officers were arrested in the purges. Releasing those who can still serve and returning "
        "them to command will give the army back some of the talent it has lost.",
    "SOV_desperate_measures":
        "When the enemy is at the gates, ordinary rules no longer apply. Calling up older men, workers' militias "
        "and every reserve the state can find may yet save the motherland.",
    "SOV_socialism_in_one_country":
        "World revolution can wait; first socialism must be built and defended here, in the Soviet Union. "
        "Concentrating our strength on our own country will make it an unbreakable fortress.",
    "SOV_the_stalin_constitution":
        "The new constitution of 1936 promises universal suffrage, civil rights and equality for all the peoples "
        "of the Union. Whatever its limits in practice, it will strengthen the authority of the Soviet state at "
        "home and abroad.",
    "SOV_nkvd_primacy":
        "The People's Commissariat for Internal Affairs controls the police, the border troops and the labour "
        "camps. Making it the dominant force in the state guarantees obedience - at the price of fear in every "
        "office and factory.",
    "SOV_expand_the_agitprop":
        "Posters, films, newspapers and lectures carry the Party's message to every village. More funding for "
        "agitation and propaganda will keep the people united behind the leadership and its plans.",
    "SOV_the_new_soviet_woman":
        "Women make up half of the Soviet workforce and drive tractors, build machines and fly aircraft. "
        "Celebrating their role, with nurseries and equal pay, will strengthen the economy and the loyalty of "
        "millions.",
    "SOV_development_aid_for_eastern_allies":
        "Mongolia and Tannu Tuva are our closest friends in Asia. Aid for their industry, schools and armies will "
        "strengthen them as buffers against Japan and as examples of socialist development.",
    "SOV_send_military_advisors_to_spain":
        "The Spanish Republic is fighting for its life against Franco's fascists, who are backed by Germany and "
        "Italy. Sending tanks, aircraft and advisors will help the Republic and give our officers experience in "
        "modern war.",
    "SOV_policy_of_collective_security":
        "Fascism threatens us and the Western democracies alike. Working with Britain and France through the "
        "League of Nations, and signing treaties of mutual assistance, may stop Hitler before he grows too "
        "strong.",
    "SOV_policy_of_individual_security":
        "The Western democracies would be happy to see us fight Germany alone. We will look after our own "
        "security first, signing agreements with whoever serves Soviet interests best.",
    "SOV_baltic_security":
        "Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania could become a gateway for an attack on Leningrad. Treaties of mutual "
        "assistance and Soviet bases on their soil would close that gateway.",
    "SOV_middle_east_diplomacy":
        "Turkey, Iran and Afghanistan border the Soviet south. Good relations with them, built on trade and "
        "treaties of friendship, will keep the British out of our backyard.",
    "SOV_the_threat_from_the_land_of_the_rising_sun":
        "Japan has already seized Manchuria and is pushing deeper into China. The Far East must be prepared for "
        "war, and China helped in its struggle, before the Japanese turn north against us.",
    "SOV_reconcile_japan":
        "A war in the east would weaken us in the west, where the greater danger lies. A neutrality treaty with "
        "Tokyo would let both sides turn their attention elsewhere.",
    "SOV_increase_state_reserves":
        "In a long war, the state must be able to feed its people and supply its factories. Building up reserves "
        "of grain, fuel and strategic metals now will carry us through the hardest years.",
    "SOV_eastern_development":
        "Siberia and Central Asia hold vast natural wealth that has barely been touched. New towns, mines and "
        "power stations in the east will spread industry across the whole Union.",
    "SOV_develop_the_urals":
        "The Urals are rich in iron, coal and metals and lie safely far from any border. Building new steel works "
        "and machine plants there will create a second industrial heart for the country.",
    "SOV_increase_aircraft_production":
        "Quantity has a quality of its own. Simplifying designs and running the factories day and night will give "
        "the air force more planes than any enemy can shoot down.",
    "SOV_intensify_pilot_training_program":
        "A plane without a skilled pilot is just a target. Longer courses, more flying hours and experienced "
        "instructors will produce pilots able to match the best of the enemy.",
    "SOV_raskovas_aviation_group":
        "Marina Raskova, the famous navigator, wants to form regiments flown entirely by women. Her aviation "
        "group will train fighter, bomber and night bomber crews and prove their courage in battle.",
    "SOV_surface_warfare":
        "Destroyers, cruisers and battleships will form the core of the Red Fleet. A strong surface force can "
        "protect our coasts and support the army's flanks along the sea.",
    "SOV_submarine_warfare":
        "Submarines are the most effective weapon for a navy that cannot match the enemy's battleships. A large "
        "submarine fleet can defend our coasts and attack enemy shipping in every sea.",
    "SOV_soviet_artillery":
        "Artillery is the god of war, Comrade Stalin says. More guns, heavier calibres and rocket launchers in "
        "great numbers will give the Red Army overwhelming firepower.",
    "SOV_pc_of_mortar_armament":
        "Mortars are cheap, simple and deadly in the hands of infantry. A commissariat devoted to them will flood "
        "the army with light and heavy mortars and give every rifle battalion its own artillery.",
    "SOV_development_of_tankograd":
        "Chelyabinsk, beyond the Urals, can become a city of tank factories - a Tankograd. Concentrating tank and "
        "engine production there will keep it safe from bombers, though moving the experts east weakens our "
        "defences for a time.",
    "SOV_the_defense_of_moscow":
        "Moscow is the heart of the Union, its capital and its greatest railway hub. Rings of trenches, anti-tank "
        "ditches and fortified villages around the city will make it the rock on which any invader breaks.",
    "SOV_impregnable_forts":
        "The fortified districts along the border must become true fortresses. Heavy concrete, interlocking "
        "fields of fire and underground galleries will hold out even when cut off and surrounded.",
    "SOV_protect_the_white_sea_baltic_canal":
        "The canal from Leningrad to the White Sea lets warships move between the Baltic and the Arctic without "
        "passing foreign coasts. Defending its locks and approaches keeps that route open for the fleet.",
    "SOV_an_adaptable_army":
        "The war has shown that rigid plans fail on the modern battlefield. Commanders who are allowed to adapt, "
        "to retreat when needed and to strike when they see a chance, will win where blind obedience loses.",
    "SOV_lessons_of_war":
        "Every battle, won or lost, teaches something. Studying our campaigns honestly and spreading the lessons "
        "through new manuals and training will make the Red Army better with each passing month.",
    "SOV_penal_battalions":
        "Soldiers and officers convicted by military tribunals can redeem themselves in penal units at the most "
        "dangerous points of the front. It is a cruel measure, but it adds men to the line at the hardest "
        "moments.",
    "SOV_the_zinovyevite_terrorist_center":
        "Zinoviev and Kamenev, once Lenin's closest comrades, stand accused in a great public trial of plotting "
        "against the leadership. Their confessions will be used to justify a purge of all the Party's supposed "
        "enemies.",
    "SOV_positive_heroism":
        "The people need heroes to follow: pilots, explorers, record-breaking workers. Celebrating individual "
        "achievements in the press and on the screen will inspire millions to give their best.",
    "SOV_collectivist_propaganda":
        "No single person is greater than the collective. Propaganda that praises the brigade, the factory and "
        "the kolkhoz over the individual will strengthen discipline and bring more volunteers into the ranks.",
    "SOV_the_komsomol":
        "The Young Communist League reaches millions of young people in schools, factories and villages. Giving "
        "it a bigger role will train the next generation of Party members, soldiers and workers.",
    "SOV_war_measures_in_the_east":
        "Japan's armies stand along the borders of Mongolia and the Soviet Far East. Moving reinforcements, "
        "aircraft and supplies east will prepare us for a conflict that could break out at any time.",
    "SOV_anti_fascist_policies":
        "Fascism is the most dangerous enemy of the working class. Supporting anti-fascist movements abroad and "
        "popular fronts with socialists and democrats will rally the world against Berlin and Rome.",
    "SOV_anti_capitalist_policies":
        "The capitalist states are all our enemies, whatever their flag. We will rely on the strength of the "
        "Soviet people and make no lasting alliances with London, Paris or Washington.",
    "SOV_respect_baltic_self_determination":
        "The independence of Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania can be respected - as long as they remain friendly "
        "towards Moscow. Good relations will make them a shield for Leningrad rather than a threat.",
    "SOV_claims_in_baltic":
        "The Baltic states were part of the Russian Empire for two centuries and lie across the approaches to "
        "Leningrad. Bringing them into the Union, by pressure or by force, will close that door for good.",
    "SOV_the_southern_thrust":
        "Iran and the Middle East lie on our southern border, with oil and access to the Indian Ocean. Expanding "
        "our influence southward would challenge British power in the region.",
    "SOV_support_afghan_ideology":
        "Afghanistan is poor and divided, but its people have long resisted the British. Supporting progressive "
        "forces there will build a friendly neighbour on our Central Asian border.",
    "SOV_the_gobi_gambit":
        "Mongolia is our closest ally in Asia and a barrier between Japanese Manchuria and Siberia. Investing in "
        "its roads, railways and army will turn the Gobi into a fortress against Japan.",
    "SOV_two_red_flags":
        "Mao Zedong's Chinese communists are fighting both the Kuomintang and the Japanese. Supporting them "
        "directly would build a second socialist state in Asia - and a long war on the Kuomintang's flank.",
    "SOV_support_the_kuomintang":
        "Chiang Kai-shek is no friend of communism, but his armies are holding back Japan. Sending him aircraft, "
        "weapons and advisors will keep the Japanese bogged down in China instead of turning north.",
    "SOV_spheres_of_influence_in_china":
        "If we reconcile with Japan, China can be divided into spheres where each side does as it pleases. "
        "Northern China and Xinjiang would fall within ours.",
    "SOV_reorganize_the_pc_of_heavy_industry":
        "The People's Commissariat of Heavy Industry has grown too large to manage. Splitting it into specialised "
        "commissariats for each branch will make planning sharper and production more efficient.",
    "SOV_shift_to_armaments_production":
        "The international situation leaves us no choice: civilian production must give way to weapons. Factories "
        "that made tractors and cars will now turn out tanks, guns and aircraft.",
    "SOV_the_ussr_academy_of_sciences":
        "The Academy of Sciences unites the best Soviet scientists. Moving branches of it to the Urals and "
        "Siberia, and setting it to work on practical problems of industry, will speed up our technical progress.",
    "SOV_merge_aircraft_plants":
        "Aircraft production is spread across too many small plants. Merging them into large factories with "
        "shared tooling and supply will raise output and make modern production methods possible.",
    "SOV_ground_support":
        "Our air force should fight above the Red Army, not far behind enemy lines. Ground-attack aircraft like "
        "Ilyushin's armoured designs will smash enemy tanks and columns right where the battle is decided.",
    "SOV_long_range_aircraft":
        "Long-range bombers can reach the enemy's industry and cities far behind the front. Building a strong "
        "force of them will give us a strategic weapon that can strike anywhere in Europe or Asia.",
    "SOV_merge_naval_plants":
        "The shipyards of the Union are scattered and poorly coordinated. Combining them into larger enterprises "
        "under a single management will let us build more ships, more quickly.",
    "SOV_offensive_maritime_strategy":
        "A fleet that only defends its harbours will never win a war. Heavy cruisers and battlecruisers able to "
        "seek out the enemy at sea will give the Red Fleet real striking power.",
    "SOV_an_oceangoing_navy":
        "A true great power needs a navy that can sail any ocean. Modern battleships of the Sovetsky Soyuz class, "
        "if we can finish them, would give the Soviet Union a fleet to match its size.",
    "SOV_mine_warfare":
        "Mines are cheap and patient, and the narrow seas around our coasts are ideal for them. Minefields and "
        "the ships to lay and clear them will protect our harbours and our convoys.",
    "SOV_long_range_raiders":
        "Large submarines with the range to reach distant shipping lanes can strike the enemy's trade far from "
        "our shores. A fleet of them would force the enemy to spread its escorts thin.",
    "SOV_merge_tank_and_materiel_plants":
        "Tank, artillery and vehicle production share engines, steel and skilled workers. Merging these plants "
        "into combined works will let them use their resources far more efficiently.",
    "SOV_leningrad_polytechnical_institute":
        "The Leningrad Polytechnic trains many of the engineers who design our weapons and machines. Expanding it "
        "and linking it to the factories will turn more of its research into practical results.",
    "SOV_military_reorganization":
        "The Red Army must be reorganised for modern war. Larger mechanised corps, better communications and a "
        "clear chain of command will help it fight as a single, coordinated force.",
    "SOV_organization_of_the_partisans":
        "If the enemy takes our land, the people must fight on behind his lines. Hidden stores of weapons, "
        "trained organisers and radio links to Moscow will turn occupied territory into a second front.",
    "SOV_smersh":
        "Death to spies - that is the name of our new counter-intelligence directorate. SMERSH will hunt down "
        "enemy agents, deserters and traitors in the army and behind the front.",
    "SOV_secure_the_administration":
        "With the conspirators unmasked, the state apparatus must be filled with reliable cadres. New officials, "
        "promoted from below and loyal to the leadership, will take the places of the purged.",
    "SOV_revive_the_stakhanovite_movement":
        "Aleksei Stakhanov cut over a hundred tonnes of coal in a single shift. Celebrating and rewarding workers "
        "who beat their norms will push others to follow their example.",
    "SOV_socialist_emulation":
        "Brigades, factories and whole cities can compete to fulfil the plan first. Organising socialist "
        "competition across the country will turn production into a matter of collective pride.",
    "SOV_annex_tannu_tuva":
        "Tannu Tuva is a small people's republic wedged between Mongolia and Siberia. Bringing it into the Union "
        "would secure its gold and uranium and remove a weak point on our border.",
    "SOV_fortify_mongolian_border":
        "Mongolia's eastern border faces the Japanese in Manchuria. Fortifications, airfields and Soviet troops "
        "along the Khalkhin Gol will protect our ally and our own flank.",
    "SOV_seek_a_defense_pact_with_the_allies":
        "A military alliance with Britain and France would surround Germany on both sides. If the democracies are "
        "serious, we are ready to sign a pact that commits all of us to fight together.",
    "SOV_approach_germany":
        "The Western powers would gladly let us bleed against Germany while they watch. An understanding with "
        "Berlin may buy us time to prepare - and perhaps some territory as well.",
    "SOV_recover_alaska":
        "The Tsar sold Alaska to the United States for a pittance in 1867. Raising a claim to it again is a "
        "provocation, but it reminds the Americans that Russia was once on their continent.",
    "SOV_secure_leningrad":
        "Leningrad lies only thirty kilometres from the Finnish border. If Helsinki will not give us land and "
        "bases to protect the city, we must take them by force.",
    "SOV_claims_on_poland":
        "The eastern half of Poland is home to millions of Ukrainians and Belarusians, and was taken from Soviet "
        "Russia in 1921. The time may come to bring these lands back into the Union.",
    "SOV_preemptive_invasion_of_iran":
        "If Iran falls under German influence, the oil of Baku and the routes to the south are in danger. "
        "Occupying it first, perhaps together with Britain, would secure our flank and a supply route from the "
        "Persian Gulf.",
    "SOV_intervention_in_china":
        "China's war with Japan offers us a chance to shape its future. Soviet troops and advisors sent into "
        "China can tip the balance and secure our influence there for decades.",
    "SOV_prepare_a_war_with_japan":
        "Sooner or later we must settle the score with Japan. Building up forces, supplies and plans in the Far "
        "East will let us strike when the moment is right.",
    "SOV_steel_casting_industry":
        "Large steel castings are needed for tank turrets, ship parts and heavy machinery. New foundries with "
        "modern methods will give industry the castings it needs in far greater numbers.",
    "SOV_the_modern_war_in_the_skies":
        "Air power is changing every aspect of war. Radar, radio-guided fighters and better tactics, learned from "
        "Spain and China, will make our air force a modern, flexible weapon.",
    "SOV_advanced_maneuvers":
        "A fleet learns by sailing. Large exercises at sea, with all types of ships working together, will teach "
        "our officers and crews to fight as one force.",
    "SOV_the_road_of_life":
        "If Leningrad is ever besieged, the frozen surface of Lake Ladoga can become a road for supplies. "
        "Preparing routes, vehicles and depots now may one day save the city from starvation.",
    "SOV_experts_in_camouflage":
        "Concealment is a weapon. Training every unit to hide its positions, use decoys and move only at night "
        "will keep the enemy guessing where our blows will fall.",
    "SOV_keep_commissars_organization":
        "The political commissars make sure that every unit stays loyal to the Party. Keeping them alongside the "
        "commanders preserves political control of the army, even if it sometimes slows down decisions.",
    "SOV_adjoined_battle_priests":
        "The Orthodox faith still lives in the hearts of many soldiers. Allowing priests to serve with the "
        "troops, as the state's relations with the Church soften, may strengthen morale in the hardest battles.",
    "SOV_swap_to_political_advisors":
        "Instead of commissars with equal authority, each unit can have a political deputy who advises but does "
        "not command. The commanders gain full control, while the Party keeps its voice in every regiment.",
    "SOV_barrier_troops":
        "Units that break and run can lose a whole front. Blocking detachments behind the line, with orders to "
        "stop retreating soldiers by any means, will force the army to stand - a measure as feared as it is "
        "effective.",
    "SOV_the_collectivization_process":
        "The collective farms must be completed and made productive, freeing millions of peasants for the "
        "factories. The cost has already been terrible, and pressing on will cost the state goodwill and the "
        "people's patience.",
    "SOV_the_anti_soviet_trotskyist_center":
        "A second great trial will expose Pyatakov, Radek and others as agents of the exiled Trotsky. Their "
        "condemnation will widen the purge into industry and the commissariats.",
    "SOV_war_heroes":
        "Pilots, tank crews and snipers who distinguish themselves in battle will be made Heroes of the Soviet "
        "Union. Their stories in every newspaper will show ordinary citizens what courage looks like.",
    "SOV_socialist_realism":
        "Art, literature and film must serve the building of socialism. Novels of heroic workers and films of "
        "collective triumph will inspire the people and strengthen their faith in the future.",
    "SOV_the_khakimov_proposal":
        "Karim Khakimov, our envoy in Arabia, argues that the Soviet Union can win friends in the Arab world by "
        "trading fairly where the British only exploit. Following his advice would open a new front of influence "
        "in the Middle East.",
    "SOV_the_fight_for_the_pacific":
        "Our Pacific coast faces Japan and America across the ocean. Expanding the ports, industry and naval "
        "forces of the Far East will make the Soviet Union a true Pacific power.",
    "SOV_demand_eastern_poland":
        "The lands east of the Curzon Line are home to Ukrainians and Belarusians who should be united with their "
        "Soviet republics. A firm demand, backed by the Red Army, will bring them back.",
    "SOV_offer_poland_protection":
        "Poland lies between us and Germany. Offering it a guarantee against German aggression would turn a "
        "hostile neighbour into a buffer - if Warsaw is willing to trust Moscow.",
    "SOV_claim_on_bessarabia":
        "Romania took Bessarabia in 1918 while Russia was torn by civil war. The Soviet Union has never accepted "
        "that loss, and the time to demand its return may be approaching.",
    "SOV_end_the_khalkhin_gol_conflict":
        "The clashes with Japan on the Mongolian border have shown that the Red Army can beat the Japanese. A "
        "decisive victory followed by a ceasefire will secure the east while we turn our attention west.",
    "SOV_recover_the_kuril_islands":
        "The Kurils and southern Sakhalin were lost to Japan, and they close our access to the Pacific. "
        "Recovering them would open the ocean to the Soviet fleet.",
    "SOV_synthetic_rubber":
        "Soviet chemists produced the world's first industrial synthetic rubber, from alcohol. Building more "
        "plants will free the army's tyres and seals from dependence on foreign rubber.",
    "SOV_oil_production":
        "Baku produces most of our oil, and it lies dangerously close to the border. Developing new fields "
        "between the Volga and the Urals - a second Baku - will keep the tanks running even if the Caucasus is "
        "threatened.",
    "SOV_found_the_jet_institute":
        "Rocket and jet engines will be the future of aviation. A research institute devoted to reactive "
        "propulsion will make sure Soviet aircraft are not left behind.",
    "SOV_expand_the_morskaya_aviatsiya":
        "Naval aviation can guard our coasts and attack enemy fleets far out at sea. Expanding it - and perhaps "
        "one day building aircraft carriers - will give the Red Fleet a long reach.",
    "SOV_naval_infantry":
        "Sailors trained to fight on land can defend naval bases and lead landings on enemy coasts. Forming naval "
        "infantry brigades will give the fleet its own assault troops.",
    "SOV_soviet_atomic_bomb_project":
        "Physicists such as Kurchatov believe that splitting the uranium atom could release unimaginable power. A "
        "secret research programme will make sure the Soviet Union is not left defenceless against such a weapon.",
    "SOV_the_glory_of_the_red_army":
        "The Red Army defeated fourteen foreign interventions in the civil war. Honouring its traditions and its "
        "victories will give every soldier pride in his uniform.",
    "SOV_the_glory_of_the_red_army_alt":
        "From Tsaritsyn to the gates of Warsaw, the Red Army's past is a story of courage against all odds. "
        "Teaching that history to every recruit will forge an army that believes it cannot be beaten.",
    "SOV_the_workers_dictatorship":
        "The dictatorship of the proletariat, led by the Party, is the guarantee of the revolution. All power "
        "must remain in the hands of the workers' state, whatever the cost to those who stand against it.",
    "SOV_patriarch_of_all_russia":
        "The Orthodox Church has been persecuted for twenty years, but it still holds the loyalty of millions. "
        "Allowing the election of a new Patriarch would win their support for the war effort.",
    "SOV_eradicate_western_fascism":
        "Fascism has spread across the West, and the capitalist democracies have done little to stop it. The Red "
        "Army, together with our allies, must carry the struggle to the heart of Europe.",
    "SOV_liberation_of_the_european_proletariat":
        "The workers of Europe groan under capitalist and fascist rule alike. When the time is right, the Red "
        "Army will march west to free them.",
    "SOV_control_scandinavia":
        "With Finland under control, the Scandinavian peninsula lies open. Bringing it into our sphere would "
        "secure the northern approaches and the iron ore of Sweden.",
    "SOV_demand_balkan_submission":
        "With Bessarabia recovered, the Balkan states must accept our leadership. Firm demands, backed by the "
        "threat of force, will bring them into line.",
    "SOV_seek_balkan_cooperation":
        "The Slavic peoples of the Balkans have long looked to Russia for protection. Treaties of friendship and "
        "trade will win them over without the need for threats.",
    "SOV_soviet_japanese_pact_against_usa_focus":
        "America's power in the Pacific threatens both Japan and the Soviet Union. A common front with Tokyo "
        "against Washington would reshape the balance of power in the whole region.",
    "SOV_industrial_modernization":
        "Old machines and outdated methods hold back our industry. Replacing them with modern equipment and "
        "training workers in new techniques will raise productivity across the economy.",
    "SOV_optimize_production_lines":
        "Armament factories can produce far more if their production lines are organised scientifically. Time "
        "studies, standardised parts and continuous flow will squeeze more weapons out of every plant.",
    "SOV_national_academies_of_sciences":
        "Each republic of the Union deserves its own academy of sciences. Building them will spread research "
        "across the country and train scientists in every corner of the Soviet Union.",
    "SOV_organization_centralization_discipline":
        "The Party, the state and the economy must answer to a single centre, with iron discipline at every "
        "level. Only then can the country be steered through the dangers ahead.",
    "SOV_the_military_conspiracy":
        "Marshal Tukhachevsky and other commanders are accused of plotting with Germany against the Soviet state. "
        "Their arrest will begin a purge that tears through the officer corps of the Red Army.",
    "SOV_restoration_and_development":
        "The war has damaged much of our industry and infrastructure. Restoring what was destroyed and building "
        "anew will take years, and for a while production will suffer.",
    "SOV_war_economy":
        "The economy must be put entirely on a war footing. Civilian needs come last; every factory, mine and "
        "farm must serve the front.",
    "SOV_the_bloc_of_rights_and_trotskyites":
        "Bukharin, Rykov and their associates face the last and greatest of the show trials. Their conviction "
        "will silence any remaining opposition within the Party.",
    "SOV_behead_the_snake":
        "The conspiracy must be destroyed at its root. Removing the leaders of the plot before they can strike "
        "will save the Union from betrayal - or so the leadership insists.",
    "SOV_fourth_five_year_plan":
        "With peace restored, the Fourth Five-Year Plan will rebuild the country and push it to new heights of "
        "industrial power. Ruined cities, flooded mines and burned villages must be rebuilt, and new industry "
        "raised beyond what was lost.",
    "SOV_stalins_cult_of_personality":
        "Portraits, statues and songs everywhere praise the leader. Building his image as the wise father of the "
        "nation will make his word unquestionable.",
    "SOV_found_the_comecon":
        "The socialist countries of Europe can coordinate their economies under Soviet leadership. A council for "
        "mutual economic assistance will tie their industries to ours.",
    "SOV_the_common_economic_space_initiative":
        "A common economic space, with shared planning and trade between the socialist states, will make all of "
        "them stronger and less dependent on the capitalist world.",
    "SOV_no_time_for_peace":
        "The capitalist world will not leave us in peace. Even after victory, research and industry must keep "
        "preparing for the next war.",
    "SOV_transformation_of_nature":
        "Forest belts across the steppe, new canals and great dams can change the climate and the land itself. "
        "This grand plan will protect the harvest from drought and make the desert bloom.",
    "SOV_transformation_of_nature_alt":
        "Soviet science can tame rivers, irrigate deserts and plant forests where none grew. Harnessing nature on "
        "a vast scale will feed the people and power the factories of the future.",
    "SOV_they_will_know_fear":
        "Our enemies must understand that any attack on the Soviet Union will be met with overwhelming force. "
        "Displays of military strength will make them think twice.",
    "SOV_inheritor_of_the_mantle_of_lenin":
        "The leader is presented as Lenin's true heir, the man who carries the revolution forward. This image "
        "will rally the people behind him in war.",
    "SOV_the_faithful_servant_of_lenin":
        "Rather than a god, the leader can be shown as the humble servant of Lenin's cause. This modest image "
        "will win respect from Party members wary of excessive worship.",
    "SOV_freedom_of_debate_unity_of_action":
        "Lenin's principle was free discussion before a decision, and complete unity once it is taken. Restoring "
        "real debate within the Party may bring better decisions and renewed support.",
    "SOV_found_the_warsaw_pact":
        "The socialist states must stand together against the threat from the West. A military alliance under "
        "Soviet command will bind their armies to ours.",
    "SOV_brilliant_genius":
        "The leader is portrayed as a genius in every field, from linguistics to military strategy. His supposed "
        "infallibility will give his decisions unquestioned authority.",
    "SOV_leader_of_the_party_and_the_people":
        "The leader stands at the head of both the Party and the nation. His authority is total, and every "
        "citizen looks to him for direction.",
    "SOV_ban_excessive_hero_worship":
        "The cult around a single person goes against the collective spirit of socialism. Curbing excessive "
        "praise will restore the authority of the Party as a whole.",
    "SOV_great_commander":
        "The leader is presented as the supreme military commander, the architect of victory. His image will "
        "inspire the soldiers at the front.",
    "SOV_architect_of_communism":
        "The leader will be remembered as the man who built communism in one country. Emphasising his role in "
        "construction rather than war will promote peaceful development.",
    "SOV_the_construction_of_communism":
        "The goal of all our efforts is the construction of a communist society of abundance. Every plan and "
        "every sacrifice brings that day closer.",
    "SOV_father_of_nations":
        "The leader is the father of all the peoples of the Union, from the Baltic to the Pacific. Uniting them "
        "under his image will bring millions more into the service of the state.",
    # British Empire
    "crypto_bomb_focus":
        "Polish mathematicians have shown that the German Enigma cipher can be broken with the help of machines. "
        "Building our own electromechanical 'bombes' at Bletchley Park would let us read the enemy's orders "
        "almost as soon as they are sent.",
    "limited_rearmament_focus":
        "The country is weary of war and wary of spending, but the dictators are arming fast. A measured "
        "rearmament programme, paid for without wrecking the budget, will begin to close the gap without alarming "
        "the Treasury or the voters.",
    "uk_empire_focus":
        "The Empire covers a quarter of the globe and is the source of Britain's strength. Strengthening its "
        "garrisons, ports and links with London will keep it together through whatever storms are coming.",
    "ENG_revisit_colonial_policy":
        "Nationalist movements in India, Egypt and elsewhere grow stronger every year. Rethinking how we govern "
        "our colonies - with more local self-rule and less coercion - may keep their loyalty better than force "
        "ever could.",
    "ENG_steady_as_she_goes":
        "Britain does not need to rush into anything. A calm, steady course through the crises of Europe, keeping "
        "our options open and our finances sound, is the best way to protect the nation's interests.",
    "air_defense_focus":
        "The bomber will always get through, they say - unless we can find it and meet it in time. Fighter "
        "squadrons, anti-aircraft guns and a network of observers will give London and the industrial cities a "
        "chance to defend themselves.",
    "shadow_scheme_focus":
        "The motor industry can build aircraft and engines if the government equips it to do so. Shadow "
        "factories, built at public expense and run by firms like Austin and Rootes, will stand ready to switch "
        "to war production overnight.",
    "ENG_motorized_focus":
        "The British Army was the first in the world to experiment with a fully mechanised force. Replacing "
        "horses with lorries and carriers across the army will make our small expeditionary force fast enough to "
        "matter.",
    "ENG_expand_the_secret_intelligence_service_focus":
        "The Secret Intelligence Service has been starved of money for years. More agents in the capitals of "
        "Europe, and better links with friendly services, will tell us what the dictators are planning before "
        "they act.",
    "general_rearmament_focus":
        "Hitler's Germany is rearming at a terrifying pace, and limited measures are no longer enough. A full "
        "rearmament programme for all three services must begin now, whatever it does to the budget.",
    "uk_service_focus":
        "Garrisons in India, Egypt, Malta and Singapore protect the arteries of the Empire. Rotating units and "
        "ships overseas regularly will give them experience and show the flag where it matters.",
    "ENG_guide_the_colonies":
        "The colonies cannot be held down forever. Guiding them patiently towards self-government, through local "
        "councils and trained administrators, can make them partners of Britain rather than reluctant subjects.",
    "ENG_global_defense":
        "Our interests stretch from the Atlantic to the Pacific, and the Royal Navy must be ready to defend them "
        "everywhere. Stronger naval bases around the world will let the fleet reach any trouble spot quickly.",
    "ENG_home_defence":
        "Whatever happens elsewhere, the British Isles must be safe. Concentrating on home defence - the fleet in "
        "home waters, the fighters over southern England and a strong army at home - will protect the heart of "
        "the Empire.",
    "radar_focus":
        "Robert Watson-Watt has shown that radio waves bouncing off aircraft can reveal them long before they "
        "come into sight. A chain of radar stations along the coast would give our fighters precious minutes of "
        "warning.",
    "uk_industrial_focus":
        "British industry is old and slow to change. Modernising factories, training skilled workers and "
        "encouraging new industries like electronics and aircraft will strengthen the economy for the years "
        "ahead.",
    "ENG_tank_focus":
        "The tank was a British invention, but others have since overtaken us. New designs - fast cruiser tanks "
        "for manoeuvre and heavily armoured infantry tanks for the assault - must be developed and built in "
        "numbers.",
    "ENG_special_air_service":
        "Small teams of highly trained men, operating deep behind enemy lines, can destroy aircraft on the "
        "ground, cut supply lines and spread confusion. Such a special force would strike where the enemy feels "
        "safest.",
    "uk_colonial_focus":
        "Educated local elites can run the colonies more efficiently than British officials alone. Training them "
        "in our universities and giving them a share in government will build loyalty and develop colonial "
        "economies.",
    "uk_mediterranean_focus":
        "The Mediterranean is the Empire's shortest route to India, through Gibraltar, Malta and the Suez Canal. "
        "Strengthening these bases will keep the route open in the face of Italian ambitions.",
    "ENG_towards_dominion_independence":
        "Canada, Australia, New Zealand and South Africa are already self-governing. Granting them full "
        "independence within the Commonwealth, as the Statute of Westminster allows, will make their support "
        "truly voluntary - and stronger for it.",
    "ENG_withdraw_from_contested_territories":
        "Some imperial possessions cost more to hold than they are worth. Withdrawing from places where our "
        "presence causes nothing but trouble would free troops for more important tasks.",
    "ENG_every_man_will_do_his_duty":
        "Nelson's famous signal at Trafalgar still stirs British hearts. Calling on every citizen to do his duty "
        "in the hour of danger will rally the nation behind the war effort.",
    "ENG_motion_of_no_confidence":
        "If the government continues to appease the dictators, Parliament may lose patience. A motion of no "
        "confidence could bring down the cabinet and put a war leader in Downing Street.",
    "uk_iraq_focus":
        "Iraq is nominally independent, but its oil and its airfields are vital to the Empire. If a hostile "
        "government comes to power in Baghdad, we must be ready to restore our position by force.",
    "uk_scandinavian_focus":
        "Germany depends on Swedish iron ore shipped through Norwegian waters. Plans for an intervention in "
        "Scandinavia could cut that supply and close the northern route to the Atlantic.",
    "ENG_prepare_for_the_inevitable":
        "War with Germany now seems unavoidable. Stockpiling materials, expanding factories and making plans for "
        "rationing will make sure the country is ready when the moment comes.",
    "ENG_benelux_intervention":
        "The Low Countries are the gateway to France and the springboard for any attack on Britain. If their "
        "neutrality cannot protect them, we may have to act first to secure them.",
    "ENG_issue_gasmasks":
        "Everyone remembers the gas attacks of the last war, and many fear they will be repeated against our "
        "cities. Issuing a gas mask to every man, woman and child will reassure the public and prepare it for the "
        "worst.",
    "tizard_mission_focus":
        "Henry Tizard proposes sharing our most secret inventions - radar, the cavity magnetron, jet engines - "
        "with the United States. In return, American factories could build them in quantities we can only dream "
        "of.",
    "uk_extra_tech_slot":
        "The research establishments at Farnborough, Malvern and Porton Down are short of staff and money. "
        "Funding them generously will give our scientists the means to work on more projects at once.",
    "air_rearmament_focus":
        "The Royal Air Force must grow quickly to match the Luftwaffe. Ordering Hurricanes, Spitfires and modern "
        "bombers in large numbers, and training the pilots to fly them, cannot wait any longer.",
    "ENG_parachute_regiments":
        "German paratroopers have shown what airborne forces can do. Setting up a depot and training school for "
        "our own parachute troops will give the army a way to strike from the sky.",
    "naval_rearmament_focus":
        "The Royal Navy is still the largest in the world, but many of its ships are old. New battleships, "
        "carriers, cruisers and destroyers must be laid down to keep it ahead of Germany, Italy and Japan.",
    "uk_asia_focus":
        "Japan threatens our possessions in the Far East. Building up industry and defences in India, Malaya and "
        "Burma will make the Empire less dependent on supplies from home.",
    "uk_commonwealth_focus":
        "The Dominions stood with Britain in the last war, and their support will be just as important in the "
        "next. Closer cooperation in trade, defence and diplomacy will strengthen the bonds of the Commonwealth.",
    "uk_rock_focus":
        "Gibraltar guards the entrance to the Mediterranean. Strengthening its fortifications, tunnelling into "
        "the Rock and adding guns will make it impregnable even if Spain turns hostile.",
    "uk_spain_focus":
        "If Spain joins the Axis, Gibraltar is in danger. Economic pressure and diplomatic threats may keep "
        "Franco out of the war - or bring him to heel.",
    "ENG_foundations_for_an_indian_state":
        "India's millions want to govern themselves, and the Government of India Act was only a first step. "
        "Laying the foundations for an Indian state, with its own industries and institutions, would turn the Raj "
        "into a partner.",
    "ENG_self_government_for_the_mediterranean":
        "Malta, Cyprus and our other Mediterranean territories could be given greater self-government. Local "
        "autonomy would reduce unrest and free some of our garrisons.",
    "ENG_self_government_for_the_middle_east":
        "Palestine, Transjordan and the Gulf states are restless under British control. Granting them more "
        "autonomy may calm nationalist movements and bring in local volunteers.",
    "ENG_no_further_appeasement":
        "Every concession to the dictators has only encouraged them to demand more. Britain will make no more "
        "concessions: the next act of aggression will be met with force.",
    "uk_iran_focus":
        "Iran's oil fields at Abadan are the largest source of fuel for the Royal Navy. If Iran leans towards "
        "Germany, we must be prepared to occupy the country to protect them.",
    "ENG_swedish_intervention":
        "Sweden's iron ore keeps Germany's war machine running. Seizing the mines of Kiruna and the port of Luleå "
        "would deal Germany a heavy blow, though it means violating Swedish neutrality.",
    "ENG_danish_intervention":
        "Denmark controls the straits between the North Sea and the Baltic. Occupying it before Germany does "
        "would keep the German fleet bottled up.",
    "ENG_belgium_security":
        "Belgium's neutrality did not save it in 1914. Securing its territory before Germany strikes may be the "
        "only way to stop the enemy reaching the Channel coast.",
    "ENG_dutch_security":
        "The Netherlands guard the mouths of the Rhine and the coast facing England. Taking control of them first "
        "would deny Germany airfields and ports within easy reach of London.",
    "ENG_military_training_act":
        "For the first time in peacetime, young men will be called up for military training. Conscription will "
        "give the army the trained reserves it will need when war comes.",
    "maud_focus":
        "Scientists Frisch and Peierls have calculated that a bomb made from uranium could be small enough to "
        "carry by aircraft. A committee to study the possibility will decide whether Britain should build such a "
        "weapon.",
    "royal_ordinance_focus":
        "The Royal Ordnance Factories produce explosives, shells and small arms for the forces. Building new "
        "factories at Chorley, Bridgend and elsewhere will multiply our munitions output.",
    "ENG_vickers_experimental_facility_focus":
        "Vickers-Armstrongs designs everything from tanks to bombers to battleships. Funding its experimental "
        "workshops will bring new weapons to the forces faster. Its engineers at Weybridge and Chertsey have more "
        "ideas than the War Office has money to test.",
    "bomber_command_focus":
        "A dedicated bomber command will plan and carry out attacks on the enemy's industry, transport and "
        "cities. Heavy bombers able to reach deep into Germany will carry the war to the enemy's homeland.",
    "ENG_chiefs_of_staff_committee":
        "The heads of the army, navy and air force must plan together, not compete for the budget. A committee of "
        "the chiefs of staff will coordinate strategy across all three services.",
    "uk_amphibious_focus":
        "One day the army will have to return to the continent from the sea. Landing craft, specialised units and "
        "joint training with the navy will make that return possible.",
    "ENG_anti_non_contact_committee":
        "Magnetic and acoustic mines explode without ever touching a ship. A committee of scientists and naval "
        "officers will develop the means to defeat them - degaussing cables, new sweeps and better minesweepers.",
    "uk_burma_focus":
        "The road from Burma into China is Chiang Kai-shek's lifeline against Japan. Building it up and keeping "
        "it open will help China fight on and keep Japan bogged down far from India.",
    "singapore_focus":
        "Singapore is the key to the Far East, the fortress where the main fleet would base in a war with Japan. "
        "Its defences and docks must be ready to receive the fleet when it sails east.",
    "hongkong_focus":
        "Hong Kong lies exposed on the coast of China, within easy reach of Japanese forces. Strengthening its "
        "garrison and defences will show that we mean to hold it, whatever the odds.",
    "uk_india_focus":
        "India has vast reserves of labour and raw materials but little modern industry. Investing in factories, "
        "railways and power stations will make it a great arsenal for the Empire.",
    "ENG_british_commonwealth_air_training_plan":
        "Canada's wide skies, safe from enemy bombers, are ideal for training pilots. A joint plan with the "
        "Dominions will train tens of thousands of aircrew for the Royal Air Force and the Commonwealth air "
        "forces.",
    "uk_australia_focus":
        "Australia has iron, coal and a skilled workforce, but most of its manufactured goods still come from "
        "Britain. Investment in steelworks, munitions plants and shipyards would make it a second arsenal of the "
        "Empire in the Pacific.",
    "uk_protect_suez":
        "The Suez Canal is the jugular vein of the Empire, through which oil, troops and trade flow between "
        "Europe and Asia. A strong garrison in Egypt and defences along the canal will keep it open against any "
        "threat.",
    "uk_malta_focus":
        "Malta lies in the middle of the Mediterranean, within easy reach of Italian airfields. Bomb-proof "
        "shelters, more fighters and stronger anti-aircraft defences will let it survive as a base for the fleet "
        "and the air force.",
    "ENG_the_three_nation_solution":
        "Hindus and Muslims in India increasingly see their futures apart. A settlement creating separate states "
        "for the main communities, with the princely states free to choose, may be the only way to avoid civil "
        "war when British rule ends.",
    "ENG_self_government_for_the_americas":
        "Our Caribbean islands, British Guiana and British Honduras are far from the centre of any war. Granting "
        "them self-government would reduce costs and win their people's goodwill, along with volunteers for the "
        "forces.",
    "ENG_kickstart_the_war_industry":
        "Appeasement is over and war may come at any moment. New arms factories, financed by emergency loans, "
        "must be built and staffed without delay.",
    "ENG_maintaining_imperial_integrity":
        "The Empire's power rests on the Royal Navy's command of the sea lanes. Keeping the fleet strong and the "
        "imperial routes secure will hold the Empire together whatever happens in Europe.",
    "ENG_maintaining_the_balance_of_power":
        "For centuries Britain has made sure that no single power dominates the continent. That policy is needed "
        "again: we must stand with those who resist the strongest power in Europe.",
    "ENG_embargo_ussr":
        "The Soviet Union's ambitions threaten its neighbours and our interests in Asia. Cutting off trade and "
        "credits to Moscow will weaken its industry and show our disapproval.",
    "ENG_norwegian_intervention":
        "Norway's long coast gives German ships and submarines a route to the Atlantic. Landing troops in Norway "
        "before the Germans do would close that route and cut off the iron ore of Narvik.",
    "ENG_embargo_germany":
        "Germany depends on imports of oil, rubber and metals. Persuading other nations to stop trading with "
        "Berlin will starve its war industry long before the first shot is fired.",
    "UK_secret_focus":
        "Britain's scientists are working on radar, jet engines and even atomic research. Concentrating funds and "
        "talent on these secret projects could give us weapons the enemy cannot match.",
    "uk_small_arms_focus":
        "The Birmingham Small Arms Company makes rifles, machine guns and motorcycles for the forces. Expanding "
        "its works will keep the army supplied with the small arms it uses in vast quantities.",
    "fighter_command_focus":
        "A single command for all fighters, linked to the radar stations and the observer corps by telephone, can "
        "direct every squadron to where it is needed most. Hugh Dowding's system will be the shield of Britain.",
    "coastal_command_focus":
        "Long-range patrol aircraft can find U-boats and surface raiders far out at sea. A dedicated coastal "
        "command, working closely with the navy, will protect the convoys from the air.",
    "uk_destroyer_focus":
        "Destroyers are the most useful ships in the fleet, escorting convoys, hunting submarines and screening "
        "the battle line. A new class built quickly and in large numbers will meet the demands of a long war at "
        "sea.",
    "uk_waves_focus":
        "Britannia rules the waves, and she must go on ruling them. A long-term naval programme, with new "
        "doctrines and modern ships, will keep the Royal Navy the first navy of the world.",
    "ENG_secure_the_imperial_shipping_routes":
        "Thousands of merchant ships sail between Britain and the Empire every year. Bases, escorts and plans to "
        "protect them will keep food, fuel and raw materials flowing to the home islands.",
    "ENG_royal_malay_regiment_focus":
        "The Royal Malay Regiment has proved that Malays make excellent soldiers. Expanding it into a larger "
        "force will help defend Malaya and give its people a stake in their own defence.",
    "ENG_territorial_army_of_malaysia_focus":
        "The volunteer forces of the Straits Settlements and the Malay states are scattered and poorly equipped. "
        "Uniting them into a single territorial army will turn them into a real defence force.",
    "uk_free_india_focus":
        "India's demand for freedom can no longer be denied. Granting full independence would end decades of "
        "struggle and might win India's goodwill for the future.",
    "ENG_indian_autonomy":
        "India can be given wide powers of self-government while remaining under the Crown. Autonomy would "
        "satisfy many nationalists without breaking the link with Britain.",
    "uk_new_zealand_focus":
        "New Zealand is small but prosperous, with dairy, wool and a growing industry. Investment in its "
        "factories and ports will help it contribute more to the Empire's strength.",
    "uk_turkey_focus":
        "Turkey controls the straits between the Black Sea and the Mediterranean. Pressure and promises may bring "
        "Ankara onto our side, or at least keep it neutral.",
    "uk_greece_focus":
        "Greece commands the eastern Mediterranean with its islands and ports. Bringing Athens firmly under our "
        "influence will protect the approaches to Suez.",
    "uk_balkan_strategy":
        "In the last war, the Balkans proved a soft underbelly of the Central Powers. A strategy of alliances and "
        "bases in the region could open a second front against our enemies.",
    "ENG_towards_indian_independence":
        "India is ready to stand on its own. A clear path to independence, with elections and a constitution, "
        "would release hundreds of thousands of Indians willing to fight beside us as allies.",
    "ENG_self_government_for_africa":
        "Nationalist movements are stirring in Nigeria, the Gold Coast and Kenya. Granting greater "
        "self-government would win their support and bring many volunteers to the Commonwealth forces.",
    "ENG_self_government_for_asia":
        "Ceylon, Burma and Malaya are moving towards self-rule. Accelerating that process will reduce the burden "
        "of empire and turn former colonies into friends.",
    "ENG_secure_the_oil_imports":
        "The oil of the Dutch East Indies could fall into enemy hands if the Netherlands are overrun. Securing "
        "those oil fields before anyone else can would protect our fuel supply in the East.",
    "ENG_enforce_the_naval_treaties":
        "The Washington and London naval treaties once limited the size of the world's fleets. Insisting that "
        "they be respected again would slow the naval build-up of our rivals.",
    "ENG_continental_intervention":
        "We cannot hide behind the Channel and let Europe fall. A strong expeditionary force, sent to the "
        "continent alongside our allies, will help stop aggression before it reaches our shores.",
    "ENG_war_with_ussr":
        "With Germany defeated, the Soviet Union may become the next threat to Europe. Planning for a war against "
        "it, while our armies are still in the field, is a precaution few would dare to speak of aloud.",
    "ENG_war_with_germany":
        "Germany has broken every promise it ever made, from the Rhineland to Prague. There is no choice left but "
        "to fight, and the sooner Britain and her allies strike, the less time Hitler has to grow stronger.",
    "aircraft_production_focus":
        "A separate ministry for aircraft production, with the power to cut through red tape, will get more "
        "planes out of the factories. Lord Beaverbrook's energy could double the output in months.",
    "uk_convoy_focus":
        "Convoys of merchant ships under naval escort defeated the U-boats in the last war. More escort vessels "
        "and more merchant ships to sail with them will keep the island fed and supplied.",
    "uk_carrier_focus":
        "Aircraft carriers can strike enemy fleets far beyond the range of any battleship's guns. Making them the "
        "core of the fleet will prepare the Royal Navy for a new kind of war at sea.",
    "uk_battleship_focus":
        "The battleship is still the backbone of naval power. New, fast and heavily armed battleships of the King "
        "George V class will keep the Royal Navy ahead of its rivals.",
    "peninsular_focus":
        "The defence of Malaya depends on holding its narrow peninsula and its jungle roads. Training troops to "
        "fight in the jungle and preparing defensive lines will make the Japanese pay for every mile.",
    "ENG_south_east_asia_air_command_focus":
        "Our air forces in the Far East are scattered and outdated. A single air command for South East Asia, "
        "with modern fighters and bombers, will defend Singapore, Malaya and Burma from the air.",
    "uk_canada_focus":
        "Canada is rich in resources and close to American industry. Developing its factories and shipyards will "
        "make it a powerhouse of the Commonwealth war effort.",
    "uk_south_africa_focus":
        "South Africa has gold, coal and a strategic position on the route around Africa. Investing in its "
        "industry will strengthen the Empire's southern anchor.",
    "uk_sanction_italy_focus":
        "Mussolini's attack on Ethiopia has shown his ambitions. Economic sanctions, enforced by the League and "
        "the Royal Navy, will make Italy pay for its aggression.",
    "ENG_decolonization":
        "The age of empire is ending. A planned withdrawal from the colonies, handing power to local governments, "
        "will leave behind friendly states instead of bitter enemies.",
    "uk_jet_focus":
        "Frank Whittle has built a working jet engine, years ahead of anything else. Developing it into a fighter "
        "aircraft could give the Royal Air Force a decisive advantage.",
    "ENG_a_s_warfare":
        "Anti-submarine warfare requires new weapons, new ships and new tactics. Better sonar, depth charges and "
        "forward-throwing weapons will turn the hunted into the hunters.",
    "ENG_expand_the_repair_yards":
        "Damaged ships must return to service quickly. More dry docks and repair yards, at home and around the "
        "Empire, will keep the fleet at sea.",
    "ENG_sarawakrangers_focus":
        "The Sarawak Rangers know the jungles of Borneo better than any outsider. Strengthening and arming them "
        "will give us local forces able to fight the Japanese on their own ground.",
    "ENG_east_indies_fleet_focus":
        "A permanent fleet in the Indian Ocean, based at Trincomalee and Singapore, will protect the routes to "
        "India and Australia and stand ready to face Japan.",
    "uk_china_focus":
        "China's war against Japan helps us by keeping the Japanese army busy. Supporting Chiang Kai-shek with "
        "credits and supplies will strengthen a valuable partner in Asia.",
    "ENG_imperial_conference":
        "Every Dominion prime minister is invited to London for a conference on defence, trade and the Empire's "
        "future. A common policy agreed around one table will strengthen every member far more than separate "
        "deals.",
    "ENG_war_with_italy":
        "Italy's aggression in the Mediterranean and Africa must be stopped. If sanctions have failed, war is the "
        "only remaining option. The Royal Navy in the Mediterranean and the army in Egypt must strike before "
        "Mussolini's forces can reinforce Libya.",
    "ENG_the_winds_of_change":
        "The wind of change is blowing through the Empire, and we must go with it rather than against it. Freed "
        "from the burden of colonial rule, Britain can rebuild its economy at home.",
    "ENG_anti_submarine_training_school":
        "Escort crews must be trained to hunt submarines as a team. A dedicated school, with realistic exercises "
        "against our own submarines, will produce skilled escort groups.",
    "ENG_vanguard":
        "HMS Vanguard, the last and greatest British battleship, can be completed with guns taken from older "
        "ships. Her addition to the fleet will be a symbol of British naval power.",
    "uk_sanction_japan_focus":
        "Japan's war in China and its threats against our possessions cannot go unanswered. Restricting exports "
        "of oil, steel and rubber to Japan will weaken its war machine.",
    "ENG_imperial_federation":
        "The Empire could become a federation of equal nations with a common parliament and defence. Such a union "
        "would make it the greatest power on earth.",
    "ENG_war_with_japan":
        "Japan has threatened our possessions for too long. With our forces in Asia strengthened, we are ready to "
        "meet its aggression with force.",
    # French Republic
    "FRA_devalue_the_franc":
        "France clung to gold long after Britain and America let their currencies fall, and our exports have paid "
        "the price. Devaluing the franc will make French goods cheap abroad again and revive industry, though "
        "savers will feel robbed.",
    "FRA_begin_rearmament":
        "Germany's army is growing every month while ours ages. A great rearmament programme, funded by special "
        "credits, must give the army modern tanks, guns and aircraft before it is too late.",
    "FRA_form_the_popular_front":
        "The riots of February 1934 showed how close the far right came to toppling the Republic. Socialists, "
        "radicals and communists, united in a Popular Front under Léon Blum, can defend democracy and bring "
        "long-overdue social reforms.",
    "FRA_naval_rearmament":
        "Italy's fleet in the Mediterranean and Germany's new ships in the North Sea both threaten our sea lanes. "
        "The Marine Nationale needs modern battleships, cruisers and destroyers to protect France and its empire.",
    "FRA_air_focus":
        "French aviation was the best in the world in 1918; today it lags behind Germany's. Orders for new "
        "aircraft, better factories and a clear doctrine will give the Armée de l'Air back its strength.",
    "FRA_invest_in_the_metropole":
        "The depression has left our industry weak and our regions neglected. Investment in the factories and "
        "towns of metropolitan France will lay the foundation for recovery.",
    "FRA_autoroutes":
        "Germany is building motorways while our roads still follow routes from the age of carriages. Modern "
        "highways between Paris and the great cities would speed trade and the movement of troops.",
    "FRA_invest_in_the_colonies":
        "The empire from Dakar to Saigon holds vast resources that France has barely used. Investing in its "
        "ports, railways and plantations will make it a real source of strength for the mother country.",
    "FRA_defensive_focus":
        "France lost a generation of young men in the last war and cannot afford another bloodbath. A strategy of "
        "defence - fortifications, firepower and careful preparation - will make any invasion fail at our "
        "borders.",
    "FRA_aggressive_focus":
        "Waiting behind walls handed the initiative to the enemy in 1914. An army trained to attack, with armour "
        "and aircraft, can carry the war onto enemy soil and protect our allies in the east.",
    "FRA_ban_the_leagues":
        "The armed leagues of the far right - the Croix-de-Feu, the Action française and their allies - fight in "
        "the streets and dream of overthrowing the Republic. Banning them will defend democracy and restore "
        "order.",
    "FRA_colonial_naval_bases":
        "Bizerte, Mers-el-Kébir, Dakar and Cam Ranh Bay guard our routes to the empire. Strengthening these bases "
        "will let the fleet operate far from home and protect the colonies.",
    "FRA_the_old_school":
        "The traditional doctrine holds that battleships and a balanced battle fleet win wars at sea. We will "
        "build heavy ships able to face the Italian and German fleets in decisive battle.",
    "FRA_the_young_school":
        "The Jeune École taught that cheap, fast ships and submarines can defeat expensive battleships. A navy of "
        "torpedo boats, destroyers and submarines will give us strength at sea without ruining the budget.",
    "FRA_fighter_focus":
        "If the enemy rules the skies over France, the army is lost. Fast modern fighters like the Dewoitine "
        "D.520, built in large numbers, will defend our cities and our soldiers.",
    "FRA_bomber_focus":
        "The best defence is to strike the enemy's airfields and factories before his bombers can take off. A "
        "strong bomber force will carry the war to the enemy from the first day.",
    "FRA_metropolitan_france":
        "The industrial north and east of France are the heart of our economy, but they lie close to the German "
        "border. Investing there - and in safer regions further south - will strengthen production.",
    "FRA_algerie_france":
        "Algeria is legally part of France, with its own départements and a large French population. Developing "
        "its industry and agriculture will turn it into a second economic base across the Mediterranean.",
    "FRA_invest_in_west_africa":
        "French West Africa stretches from Senegal to Niger, with groundnuts, cotton and new mines. Railways and "
        "ports will bring these riches to France and develop the colonies themselves.",
    "FRA_invest_in_indochina":
        "Indochina produces rubber, rice and coal, and its people are among the most skilled in the empire. "
        "Investment in its industry will make it a pillar of French power in Asia.",
    "FRA_invest_in_syria":
        "The mandates of Syria and Lebanon guard our position in the Levant. Developing their roads, oil and "
        "trade will strengthen our hold on the eastern Mediterranean.",
    "FRA_firepower_kills":
        "Pétain's lesson from Verdun is simple: firepower kills. An army built around artillery and machine guns, "
        "advancing only when the enemy has been crushed, will spend shells instead of lives.",
    "FRA_methodical_battle":
        "Modern battle must be carefully planned and tightly controlled. Advances measured in kilometres, each "
        "step prepared by artillery and supplied in advance, will avoid the costly mistakes of 1914.",
    "FRA_infantry_tanks":
        "Tanks are best used to support the infantry, crushing machine-gun nests and breaking wire. Heavily "
        "armoured tanks working closely with the foot soldiers will make every attack a success.",
    "FRA_battle_of_maneuver":
        "Colonel de Gaulle argues that a professional army of armoured divisions could break through enemy lines "
        "and win a war in weeks. France should listen to him before the Germans prove him right.",
    "FRA_air_dominance":
        "Whoever controls the air controls the battlefield. Concentrating our aircraft to win air superiority "
        "will protect our army and leave the enemy blind and exposed.",
    "FRA_reform_the_labour_laws":
        "The Matignon agreements promise workers a forty-hour week, paid holidays and collective bargaining. "
        "These reforms are a triumph for social justice, though employers warn they will slow production.",
    "FRA_intervention_in_spain":
        "Spain's Republic is fighting a military rebellion supported by Germany and Italy. Helping our sister "
        "republic with arms and volunteers could stop fascism at the Pyrenees, even if London prefers neutrality.",
    "FRA_develop_colonial_dockyards":
        "Ships damaged far from home must sail back to France for repairs. Building dockyards at Dakar, Bizerte "
        "and Saigon will let the fleet be repaired and supplied where it fights.",
    "FRA_capital_ship_focus":
        "The new Richelieu-class battleships will be among the most powerful in the world. Concentrating our "
        "resources on such ships will give France a fleet able to face any rival.",
    "FRA_carrier_focus":
        "The aircraft carrier is the warship of the future. A modern French carrier, with its own air group, "
        "would give our fleet a long-range striking power no battleship can match.",
    "FRA_undersea_combat":
        "Our submarines, including the giant Surcouf, can strike enemy shipping and warships far from home. "
        "Improving their designs and training will make them a formidable weapon.",
    "FRA_surface_combat":
        "Our large, fast destroyers are the envy of other navies. Building more of them, with better guns and "
        "torpedoes, will give the fleet a powerful and flexible surface force.",
    "FRA_heavy_fighter_focus":
        "Twin-engined fighters can escort bombers deep into enemy territory and hunt enemy bombers over our own. "
        "Designs like the Potez 63 will give the air force long-range protection.",
    "FRA_air_doctrine":
        "An air force needs a clear idea of how it will fight. A new doctrine, worked out by our airmen and "
        "tested in exercises, will tell every squadron its role in the coming war.",
    "FRA_heavy_bomber_focus":
        "Large four-engined bombers can strike the enemy's industry deep inside his country. A heavy bomber force "
        "would let France hit Germany's war economy at its source.",
    "FRA_naval_bomber_focus":
        "Bombers trained to attack ships can defend our coasts and convoys. Squadrons of naval bombers based in "
        "North Africa will keep the Italian fleet in check.",
    "FRA_industrial_expansion":
        "With investment flowing into France and Algeria, industry is ready to grow. New factories, power plants "
        "and railways will lift production across the country.",
    "FRA_colonial_industry":
        "The colonies can do more than supply raw materials. Building factories in Algeria, Indochina and West "
        "Africa will create new industrial centres safe from German bombers.",
    "FRA_infantry_focus":
        "In 1793 the Republic called the whole nation to arms and stunned the kings of Europe. A modern levée en "
        "masse, training every able man as an infantryman, will give France the numbers to hold its borders.",
    "FRA_fortification_focus":
        "The Maginot Line is the most advanced fortification in the world. Further investment in its forts, "
        "casemates and underground railways will make it truly impassable.",
    "FRA_special_forces":
        "Small units trained for raids, reconnaissance and mountain warfare can do what ordinary infantry cannot. "
        "Elite chasseurs and commandos will give the army specialists for every task.",
    "FRA_motorized_focus":
        "The army still moves at the pace of its horses. Lorries and motorised infantry will let whole divisions "
        "move quickly to where the enemy attacks.",
    "FRA_cas_focus":
        "Aircraft that attack enemy troops on the battlefield can turn the tide of a battle. Squadrons trained to "
        "support the army directly will give our soldiers help from above.",
    "FRA_nationalize_key_industry":
        "The armament industry is in the hands of a few private firms more interested in profit than in the "
        "nation's defence. Nationalising the key factories will put them at the service of the Republic.",
    "FRA_the_blum_viollette_proposal":
        "Prime Minister Blum and Maurice Viollette propose giving full French citizenship to an elite of Algerian "
        "Muslims. The reform would win loyalty in Algeria - if the settlers do not block it.",
    "FRA_review_foreign_policy":
        "Germany has torn up Versailles, Italy has invaded Ethiopia and our allies in the east doubt our resolve. "
        "France needs a clear foreign policy for the dangerous years ahead.",
    "FRA_carrier_planes":
        "A flight deck full of obsolete biplanes wins no battles. Modern carrier fighters and torpedo bombers, "
        "built for landing on a pitching deck, will give our carriers real teeth.",
    "FRA_extra_research_slot":
        "The grandes écoles - the École Polytechnique, Centrale and the Mines - train France's best engineers. "
        "More money for their laboratories will give the nation more research projects at once.",
    "FRA_military_factories":
        "New arms factories, many of them in central and southern France out of reach of German bombers, will "
        "equip the army with the weapons it needs for a long war.",
    "FRA_extra_research_slot_2":
        "Science in France is scattered among universities and institutes with little coordination. A national "
        "research centre will gather the best scientists and direct their work towards national needs.",
    "FRA_global_integration":
        "The empire's economies are still tied to France only by trade. Integrating them into a single economic "
        "area, with common planning and investment, will make the whole empire stronger.",
    "FRA_artillery_focus":
        "Napoleon massed his guns into a grand battery to smash the enemy's lines. Our modern artillery, "
        "concentrated and well supplied, will do the same to any army that attacks France.",
    "FRA_alpine_forts":
        "Italy's armies stand on the other side of the Alps. Fortifications in the passes and along the coast of "
        "Provence will make any Italian attack hopeless.",
    "FRA_fusiliers_marine":
        "The navy's own infantry, the fusiliers marins, can seize ports, defend naval bases and lead landings. "
        "Expanding them into a full division will give France an assault force from the sea.",
    "FRA_mechanized_focus":
        "Motorised infantry is not enough: troops must be able to fight from their vehicles under fire. Armoured "
        "carriers and mechanised divisions will keep pace with our tanks in battle.",
    "FRA_air_ground_cooperation":
        "Pilots and soldiers must speak the same language. Liaison officers with radios at the front and joint "
        "training will let aircraft strike exactly where the army needs them.",
    "FRA_reorganize_the_aviation_industry":
        "Our aircraft industry was nationalised into regional companies, but production is still slow. "
        "Reorganising them, with modern methods and clear orders, will multiply the output of planes.",
    "FRA_form_the_state_arsenals":
        "State-owned arsenals can produce weapons at cost and without interruption from strikes or "
        "profit-seeking. Building them up will give the Republic its own armament industry.",
    "FRA_expand_the_citizenship":
        "Millions of people in the empire serve France without being full citizens. Expanding citizenship to more "
        "of them will win their loyalty and their willingness to fight for the Republic.",
    "FRA_support_the_finns":
        "Finland is fighting bravely against the Soviet invasion. Sending volunteers, aircraft and weapons will "
        "show that France stands with small nations against aggression.",
    "FRA_rush_the_richelieus":
        "The Richelieu and Jean Bart are being built in Brest and Saint-Nazaire. Rushing them to completion will "
        "give the fleet two of the most powerful battleships afloat.",
    "FRA_prioritize_the_joffre":
        "The aircraft carrier Joffre has been ordered but progresses slowly. Giving her priority in the shipyards "
        "will give France its first modern carrier.",
    "FRA_improved_screen_ships":
        "Cruisers and destroyers screen the battle fleet and hunt the enemy's light forces. Improved designs will "
        "make them faster, better armed and more seaworthy.",
    "FRA_heavy_armor_focus":
        "The Char B1 is one of the most heavily armed and armoured tanks in the world. Building more battle tanks "
        "like it will give our attacks overwhelming weight.",
    "FRA_extend_the_maginot_line":
        "The Maginot Line stops at the Belgian border, leaving the north open. Extending it to the sea would "
        "close that gap - if Belgium agrees and the budget allows.",
    "FRA_light_medium_armor":
        "Armoured cars and light tanks give the cavalry speed and firepower. Equipping the light mechanised "
        "divisions with them will create fast forces for reconnaissance and counter-attack.",
    "FRA_flying_artillery":
        "Bombers flying close over the battlefield can strike targets that the artillery cannot reach. Using them "
        "as flying artillery will give the army fire support wherever it advances.",
    "FRA_general_work_council":
        "Employers, unions and the state must work together to plan the economy. A general council for labour "
        "will settle disputes before they become strikes and keep production moving.",
    "FRA_france_undividable":
        "France and its empire form one indivisible nation. Uniting them under a single citizenship and a single "
        "flag will make every subject a defender of France.",
    "FRA_encourage_immigration":
        "France's population has barely grown in fifty years. Welcoming workers and refugees from Italy, Spain, "
        "Poland and the empire will fill our factories and our army.",
    "FRA_confirm_eastern_commitments":
        "Our alliances with Poland, Czechoslovakia and the Little Entente are the only way to keep Germany "
        "surrounded. Confirming our commitments will reassure our allies that France will march to their aid.",
    "FRA_buy_time":
        "France is not yet ready for war. Avoiding confrontation while we rearm, even at the cost of some "
        "concessions, will buy the time we need.",
    "FRA_naval_doctrine":
        "A modern navy needs a modern doctrine. Lessons from exercises and from other navies will teach our "
        "admirals how to use their ships in the next war.",
    "FRA_division_cuirassee":
        "Armoured divisions concentrate the heavy tanks into a single striking force. Forming them now will give "
        "the army the means to break any enemy line.",
    "FRA_army_reform":
        "The army's organisation dates from the last war. Reforming it with new units, new tactics and younger "
        "commanders will prepare it for the realities of modern war.",
    "FRA_dirigisme":
        "The state must direct the economy, not leave it to the market. Planning, public investment and control "
        "of credit will steer French industry towards the nation's goals.",
    "FRA_national_champions":
        "France needs great industrial companies able to compete with the giants of Germany and America. "
        "Supporting national champions in steel, cars and aircraft will build them.",
    "FRA_french_union":
        "The empire will become a French Union of equal peoples, each with a voice in its affairs. Such a union "
        "will hold together in war far better than an empire held by force.",
    "FRA_strengthen_the_little_entente":
        "Czechoslovakia, Romania and Yugoslavia formed the Little Entente with French support. Strengthening it "
        "with new guarantees will keep a ring of allies around Germany and Hungary.",
    "FRA_revive_the_franco_polish_alliance":
        "Poland has been our ally since 1921, but the relationship has cooled. Reviving the alliance with new "
        "guarantees will keep a strong partner on Germany's eastern border.",
    "FRA_go_with_britain":
        "France cannot face Germany alone, and Britain is our most important ally. Coordinating our foreign "
        "policy with London will keep the Entente Cordiale strong.",
    "FRA_france_leads":
        "France must not always follow Britain's lead. Taking the initiative in European diplomacy, with our own "
        "alliances and policies, will restore our position as a great power.",
    "FRA_invite_yugoslavia":
        "Yugoslavia is a key member of the Little Entente and borders both Italy and Germany. Inviting it into a "
        "closer alliance will strengthen our position in the Balkans.",
    "FRA_join_the_ententes":
        "The Balkan Entente of Greece, Romania, Turkey and Yugoslavia could join the Little Entente in a broad "
        "alliance under French leadership. Together the two blocs would field dozens of divisions on Germany's "
        "and Italy's eastern flanks.",
    "FRA_foreign_guest_workers":
        "Our allies in Eastern Europe have workers to spare, and our factories need them. Guest-worker agreements "
        "will bring labour to France and strengthen our ties with the east.",
    "FRA_strengthen_government_support":
        "French governments rise and fall every few months. A stronger, more stable government with broad support "
        "in parliament will give the country the leadership it needs.",
    "FRA_arms_purchases_in_the_us":
        "American factories can build aircraft faster than ours. Buying planes and engines in the United States "
        "will fill the gaps in our air force while our own industry catches up.",
    "FRA_concessions_to_italy":
        "Mussolini can be kept away from Hitler if he is given something in Africa. Concessions to Italy, however "
        "unpleasant, may keep the two dictators apart.",
    "FRA_franco_soviet_treaty":
        "The treaty of mutual assistance with the Soviet Union would put a great power on Germany's eastern "
        "flank. Ratifying and strengthening it will make Hitler think twice before attacking anyone.",
    "FRA_invite_romania":
        "Romania's oil and grain would be vital in any war. Bringing it into a closer alliance with France will "
        "keep those resources out of German hands.",
    "FRA_defensive_strategems":
        "If war cannot be avoided, it must be fought on our terms. Careful plans for the defence of France, "
        "prepared in peace, will make the enemy attack where we are strongest.",
    "FRA_ratify_the_stresa_front":
        "At Stresa, Britain, France and Italy agreed to oppose any German attempt to change the borders of "
        "Europe. Making that front a real alliance would keep Mussolini on our side.",
    "FRA_invest_in_our_weaker_allies":
        "Our allies in the east are poorer than we are and their armies are short of modern equipment. Credits "
        "and weapons from France will make them stronger partners.",
    "FRA_coordinate_rearmament":
        "Our allies are rearming separately, often with incompatible weapons. Coordinating rearmament - with "
        "common designs, shared production and joint planning - will make our alliance far stronger.",
    # Kingdom of Italy
    "ITA_ethiopian_war_logistics_bba":
        "Our armies in Ethiopia are supplied over thousands of kilometres of sea and mountain track. Better roads "
        "from the Eritrean ports, more lorries and well-run depots will decide the campaign as much as the "
        "fighting will.",
    "ITA_italian_highways_bba":
        "Italy built the first motorway in the world, from Milan to the lakes. Extending these autostrade across "
        "the peninsula will speed trade, link north and south and show what the regime can build.",
    "ITA_army_primacy_bba":
        "Italy is first of all a land power, and the army must come first. New arms factories and priority in "
        "steel and labour will give our divisions the equipment their numbers deserve.",
    "ITA_air_innovations_bba":
        "Italian pilots and designers have won the Schneider Trophy and set world records for speed and distance. "
        "Turning that brilliance into modern combat aircraft will make the Regia Aeronautica feared again.",
    "ITA_naval_power_projection":
        "The Mediterranean is mare nostrum - our sea - and the Regia Marina must be able to command it. A modern "
        "fleet, new shipyards and a bold doctrine will challenge Britain and France in their own waters.",
    "ITA_the_abyssinian_fiasco":
        "The war in Ethiopia drags on, and the reports from the front are bleak. Admitting the setbacks honestly "
        "will dent the nation's enthusiasm, but it may be the only way to fix what has gone wrong.",
    "ITA_solid_progress":
        "Our columns are advancing steadily towards Addis Ababa. Celebrating each victory in the press will raise "
        "the regime's prestige and the nation's appetite for further glory.",
    "ITA_struggle_in_ethiopia":
        "Ethiopian resistance is fierce, and every kilometre is costly. The war is draining money and political "
        "capital that the regime can ill afford.",
    "ITA_ministry_of_italian_africa":
        "With Libya, Eritrea, Somaliland and now Ethiopia, Italy has a real African empire. A single ministry to "
        "govern and develop these lands will turn conquests into colonies.",
    "ITA_steel_industry_in_terni":
        "Terni in Umbria is the home of Italy's great steelworks, far from the coast and safe from naval guns. "
        "Expanding its furnaces and rolling mills will feed both industry and the armament works.",
    "ITA_power_plants_in_terni":
        "The rivers around Terni already drive hydroelectric plants. Building more will bring cheap power to the "
        "industries of central Italy and reduce our dependence on imported coal.",
    "ITA_railway_innovations":
        "Italian electric trains are among the fastest in the world. Electrifying more lines and modernising the "
        "network will move goods and people across Italy at record speed.",
    "ITA_fiocchi_munizioni":
        "Fiocchi of Lecco produces ammunition of excellent quality. Expanding its works and building new "
        "munitions plants will keep the army supplied in a long war.",
    "ITA_preserve_army_traditions":
        "The Italian army has a proud tradition from the Risorgimento and the Piave. Preserving its regiments, "
        "its customs and its proven methods will give our soldiers steadiness in defence.",
    "ITA_a_bandits_war":
        "In the mountains of Ethiopia and the deserts of Libya, small bands striking and vanishing have humbled "
        "regular armies. Teaching our troops to fight the same way will give them speed and cunning.",
    "ITA_citta_dell_aria":
        "At Guidonia, near Rome, a whole city of aeronautical research is rising: wind tunnels, laboratories and "
        "test airfields. This city of the air will give our designers the best facilities in Europe.",
    "ITA_expand_rome_flying_school":
        "Good aircraft need good pilots. Expanding the flying schools around Rome will train more aircrew to the "
        "high standard the Regia Aeronautica demands.",
    "ITA_intensify_torpedo_manufacturing":
        "The Whitehead torpedo works at Fiume make some of the best torpedoes in the world. Building them in "
        "greater numbers will arm our submarines, destroyers and motor torpedo boats.",
    "ITA_expand_naval_facilities":
        "The great naval bases at Taranto, La Spezia and Naples need more docks and workshops. Expanding them "
        "will let us build and maintain a larger fleet.",
    "ITA_oto_naval_guns":
        "The OTO works at La Spezia build heavy guns for our battleships. Improved designs will give the new "
        "Littorio class a firepower to match any ship afloat.",
    "ITA_servizio_informazione_militare":
        "The military intelligence service gathers information on our enemies and runs agents abroad. Expanding "
        "it will tell us what Britain and France are planning in the Mediterranean.",
    "ITA_develop_ethiopia":
        "Ethiopia is vast, mountainous and rich in land. Roads, settlements and plantations will turn it into a "
        "productive part of the empire - if its people can be pacified.",
    "ITA_develop_libya":
        "Libya's coast can be farmed and its ports improved. Bringing Italian settlers and building the great "
        "coastal road will make it Italy's fourth shore.",
    "ITA_develop_eritrea":
        "Eritrea is Italy's oldest colony and its gateway to East Africa. Developing the port of Massawa and the "
        "industries of Asmara will make it the hub of Italian Africa.",
    "ITA_develop_somaliland":
        "Italian Somaliland has long coasts and fertile river valleys. Investment in banana plantations, ports "
        "and roads will make it pay for itself.",
    "ITA_industria_della_gomma_sintetica":
        "Italy has no natural rubber, and a blockade would ground our vehicles. A synthetic rubber industry, like "
        "the one Pirelli is planning, will free us from imports.",
    "ITA_expand_foggia_farm_fields":
        "The plain of Foggia in Apulia is the granary of southern Italy. Draining and irrigating more land there "
        "will feed the nation and free workers for industry.",
    "ITA_brescia_small_arms_industry":
        "Brescia has made fine weapons for five centuries, and its Beretta and Breda works are among the best in "
        "the world. Expanding them will arm every soldier with modern rifles and machine guns.",
    "ITA_milan_comms_industry":
        "Milan's electrical firms can build radios, telephones and field equipment. Giving the army modern "
        "communications will let its units coordinate in battle.",
    "ITA_increase_artillery_production":
        "Our artillery is largely of Great War vintage, much of it taken from Austria. New guns from Ansaldo and "
        "other firms will give the army modern firepower.",
    "ITA_army_leaders":
        "An army is only as strong as its officers. Promoting talented younger commanders and sending them to "
        "study abroad will give our divisions the leadership they need.",
    "ITA_superesercito":
        "A supreme army command will coordinate the army's operations in every theatre, from the Alps to Africa, "
        "and speak with one voice in the councils of war.",
    "ITA_italian_tankettes":
        "Light tankettes like the CV-33 are cheap and fast, useful in the mountains and the colonies. Building "
        "more of them, while working on heavier designs, will give the army armoured support.",
    "ITA_reggianes_exports":
        "Reggiane builds fighters and has customers abroad. Supporting its exports will bring in foreign currency "
        "and give the firm the experience to build better aircraft for our own air force.",
    "ITA_superaereo":
        "A supreme air command will plan and direct the air war across the Mediterranean and Africa, coordinating "
        "bombers, fighters and naval aviation.",
    "ITA_diving_bombers":
        "Dive bombers can hit ships and fortifications with great accuracy. Acquiring or building them will give "
        "our air force a weapon against the Royal Navy.",
    "ITA_improve_overseas_naval_bases":
        "Tobruk, Massawa and the bases in the Dodecanese let our fleet operate far from Italy. Improving them "
        "will extend the reach of the Regia Marina across the Mediterranean and the Red Sea.",
    "ITA_milizia_marittima_di_artiglieria":
        "The coastal artillery militia mans the guns that defend our harbours. Expanding and modernising it will "
        "protect our ports from enemy raids.",
    "ITA_supermarina":
        "A supreme naval command in Rome will direct the whole fleet, using radio to control ships at sea. It "
        "will make the Regia Marina a single, coordinated force.",
    "ITA_stockpile_fuel":
        "Italy has almost no oil, and the fleet burns it in vast quantities. Building up reserves now will let "
        "our ships and aircraft fight even if supplies are cut off.",
    "ITA_forza_navale_especiale":
        "A special naval force, with transports, landing craft and marines, could seize Malta or other islands. "
        "Forming it now will give us the means to strike across the sea.",
    "ITA_triumph_in_africa_bba":
        "Ethiopia has fallen and the King of Italy is now Emperor. The triumph will be celebrated across Italy "
        "and will confirm the regime's prestige at home and abroad.",
    "ITA_regional_development":
        "With the colonies developed, their economies can support new industries. Factories in Libya and East "
        "Africa will produce for the empire and reduce the burden on Italy.",
    "ITA_strengthen_northern_industry":
        "The industrial triangle of Milan, Turin and Genoa is the heart of our economy. Concentrating investment "
        "there will bring the quickest results in production.",
    "ITA_modernize_the_mezzogiorno":
        "The south of Italy is poor, rural and backward. Modernising the Mezzogiorno with roads, irrigation and "
        "factories will unite the nation and unlock its untapped labour.",
    "ITA_investments_in_edison":
        "The Edison company dominates Italy's electricity supply. Investing in its dams and power lines will "
        "bring cheap energy to industry across the country.",
    "ITA_redirect_alfa_romeo_production":
        "Alfa Romeo builds fast cars and aircraft engines. Redirecting its production to military needs will give "
        "the armed forces engines and vehicles of high quality.",
    "ITA_vallo_alpino_del_littorio":
        "The Alpine Wall will guard every pass from France to Yugoslavia with bunkers and gun positions. No "
        "invader will cross the Alps into Italy.",
    "ITA_moschettieri_del_duce":
        "The Duce's musketeers are his personal guard, chosen from the most loyal volunteers. Expanding them will "
        "add elite troops to our forces and show the regime's strength.",
    "ITA_bersaglieri":
        "The Bersaglieri, with their plumed hats and running pace, are the pride of the Italian army. Expanding "
        "them as fast, motorised infantry will give the army a mobile striking force.",
    "ITA_self_propelled_guns":
        "Guns mounted on tank chassis can follow the armour and support it with direct fire. The Semovente will "
        "give our armoured divisions the firepower they lack.",
    "ITA_carica_di_isbuscenskij":
        "Our cavalry has shown that the charge is not dead: at the right moment, horsemen can still break an "
        "enemy line. Keeping that spirit alive will give the army a bold edge.",
    "ITA_standardization":
        "Our air force flies too many different types of aircraft. Standardising on a few good designs will "
        "simplify production, training and maintenance.",
    "ITA_specialization":
        "Each mission needs its own aircraft. Specialised designs for fighters, bombers and reconnaissance will "
        "give each squadron the best tool for its task.",
    "ITA_officers_of_the_service_role":
        "Ground crews and support officers keep the aircraft flying. Giving them proper training and status will "
        "improve the readiness of the whole air force.",
    "ITA_naval_air_coordination":
        "Our fleet has no carriers and must rely on land-based aircraft. Close coordination between Supermarina "
        "and the air force will give our ships air cover over the Mediterranean.",
    "ITA_decima_flottiglia_mas":
        "Our navy's bravest men ride slow-running torpedoes into enemy harbours at night and fix charges beneath "
        "the hulls of battleships. Expanding the Tenth Flotilla of assault craft could sink the Royal Navy's "
        "giants at anchor.",
    "ITA_incrociatori_leggeri":
        "Light cruisers are fast enough to escape anything they cannot fight. A new generation of them, armed and "
        "armoured to fight in the narrow seas around Sicily, will give the fleet speed and flexibility.",
    "ITA_incrociatori_pesanti":
        "Our Zara-class heavy cruisers are among the best protected in the world. More heavy cruisers built on "
        "that model will give the fleet a powerful force to support the battleships.",
    "ITA_expand_naval_intelligence":
        "The Royal Navy's movements from Gibraltar and Alexandria must be watched constantly. More agents, radio "
        "listening posts and code-breakers will tell Supermarina where the enemy is.",
    "ITA_cooperation_programs":
        "Other navies - the Germans, the Japanese, even old rivals - have lessons to share. Exchange programmes "
        "for officers and joint exercises will broaden the experience of our fleet.",
    "ITA_devaluate_the_lire":
        "The lira has been held at an artificially high value since Mussolini's 'quota 90'. Letting it fall will "
        "help our exports and industry, even if it hurts national pride.",
    "ITA_anglo_italian_agreements":
        "Britain and Italy share the Mediterranean, and neither wants a war there. Agreements on the status quo, "
        "on Spain and on our presence in Ethiopia could ease tensions and win recognition for the empire.",
    "ITA_topple_amhara_rulers":
        "The Amhara nobility led the resistance against us in Ethiopia. Favouring the other peoples of the empire "
        "- Oromo, Tigrayans and Somalis - will weaken their hold and divide our opponents.",
    "ITA_the_new_emperor_of_ethiopia":
        "King Victor Emmanuel III has taken the title of Emperor of Ethiopia. Presenting him as a rightful ruler "
        "will help us win over the Ethiopian notables who accept Italian rule.",
    "ITA_foreign_affairs":
        "With the empire won, Italy must decide where it stands in Europe. A clear foreign policy, between "
        "Germany's ambitions and the old Western powers, will shape the nation's future.",
    "ITA_litoranea_balbo":
        "Marshal Balbo is building a great coastal road across Libya, from Tunisia to Egypt. Completing it will "
        "tie the colony together and carry troops and supplies along the coast.",
    "ITA_prospect_for_oil":
        "Geologists suspect that oil may lie beneath the Libyan desert. A serious search, with modern drilling "
        "equipment, could free Italy from its dependence on imported fuel.",
    "ITA_polizia_dell_africa_italiana":
        "A colonial police force, Italian-led and well trained, will keep order in the empire and free the army "
        "for real war. It will draw on both Italian and local recruits.",
    "ITA_strengthen_ascari_corps":
        "The Ascari, our African soldiers from Eritrea, Somalia and Libya, have served Italy loyally for decades. "
        "Expanding their units will give the empire a large army of experienced fighters.",
    "ITA_expand_national_universities":
        "Italian universities have a long and glorious history but too little modern science. More funding for "
        "engineering and the sciences will train the specialists our industry needs.",
    "ITA_divisioni_alpine":
        "The Alpini are the finest mountain troops in the world, at home in the snow and rock of the Alps. More "
        "Alpine divisions will hold our borders and fight where no other army can.",
    "ITA_end_fiat_ansaldo_duopoly":
        "Fiat and Ansaldo share almost all orders for tanks and vehicles between them, with little competition. "
        "Opening the field to other firms will bring new ideas and better designs.",
    "ITA_modernize_ansaldo_facilities":
        "Ansaldo's works at Genoa build guns, ships and tanks. Modernising its factories with new machinery will "
        "raise the quality and quantity of our heavy weapons.",
    "ITA_long_range_aircraft":
        "Italy's possessions stretch from the Aegean to the Horn of Africa. Aircraft with the range to link them "
        "all, and to strike far into the enemy's rear, will make the empire one.",
    "ITA_bomber_designs":
        "Italian three-engined bombers like the Savoia-Marchetti SM.79 have set records for speed. New designs, "
        "with better engines and defensive guns, will keep our bomber force modern.",
    "ITA_fighter_designs":
        "Our fighter pilots love agile biplanes, but the future belongs to fast monoplanes. Designs like the "
        "Macchi C.200 and its successors must be developed and built quickly.",
    "ITA_multirole_aircraft":
        "With limited industry, Italy needs aircraft that can do many jobs well. Multi-role designs that fight, "
        "bomb and reconnoitre will make the most of every factory.",
    "ITA_cruiser_submarines":
        "Large ocean-going submarines can sail far into the Atlantic and the Indian Ocean. Building them will let "
        "our submarine fleet strike at Britain's trade far from the Mediterranean.",
    "ITA_midget_submarines":
        "Small submarines with crews of two or three can slip into defended harbours unseen. A force of them "
        "would give the navy a weapon perfectly suited to the narrow seas.",
    "ITA_cacciatorpediniere_di_scorta":
        "Our convoys to Libya need protection from British submarines and aircraft. Escort destroyers built for "
        "the task will see them safely across.",
    "ITA_ispettorato_dei_mezzi_antisommergibili":
        "An inspectorate devoted to anti-submarine warfare will develop detection gear, depth charges and "
        "tactics. It will make our convoys far harder targets for British submarines.",
    "ITA_navi_da_battaglia":
        "The new Littorio-class battleships are fast, beautiful and powerfully armed. Building more of them will "
        "give Italy a battle line to match any in the Mediterranean.",
    "ITA_proper_carriers":
        "Italy's admirals once said that the peninsula itself was an aircraft carrier. The war will prove them "
        "wrong: we need real carriers to give the fleet air cover at sea.",
    "ITA_refit_civilian_ships":
        "The great passenger liners Roma and Augustus could be converted into aircraft carriers. It is a quicker "
        "path to naval aviation than building carriers from the keel up.",
    "ITA_culto_del_duce":
        "The Duce is always right, say the posters on every wall. Building the cult of Mussolini as the father of "
        "the nation will bind the people to the regime.",
    "ITA_balkan_ambition":
        "The Balkans lie across the Adriatic from Italy, weak and divided. Expanding our influence there - by "
        "pressure or by force - will make the Adriatic an Italian lake.",
    "ITA_potential_allies_in_the_balkans":
        "Hungary, Bulgaria and others in the Balkans have grievances against their neighbours. Winning them as "
        "allies will extend Italian influence without war.",
    "ITA_corpo_di_truppe_volontarie":
        "Our volunteers are fighting for Franco in Spain. Expanding the Volunteer Troops Corps will win the civil "
        "war for the nationalists and give our army combat experience.",
    "ITA_via_della_vittoria":
        "The road of victory will extend the coastal road from Libya into Egypt, carrying our armies towards the "
        "Suez Canal. Every kilometre of asphalt laid across the desert is a kilometre our lorries need not fight "
        "through sand.",
    "ITA_libyan_refineries":
        "If oil is found in Libya, it must be refined on the spot. Building refineries near the fields will turn "
        "crude oil into fuel for the army and the fleet.",
    "ITA_comandante_diavolo":
        "Amedeo Guillet, known to his enemies as Commander Devil, leads cavalry in the highlands of Eritrea. His "
        "example of daring will inspire colonial troops and draw new recruits to our banners.",
    "ITA_new_industrialization_program":
        "A new national programme, backed by the IRI state holding company, will build up the industries that "
        "Italy still lacks: chemicals, steel and machinery.",
    "ITA_increase_production":
        "Our factories must produce more, faster. Longer shifts, simpler designs and mass production methods will "
        "raise output across the armament industry. Quality will suffer a little, but an army needs enough rifles "
        "and shells before it needs perfect ones.",
    "ITA_keep_specialization":
        "Italian craftsmanship is the best in the world. Keeping our specialised, high-quality production may "
        "mean fewer weapons, but each one will be excellent.",
    "ITA_fanti_dell_aria":
        "Paratroopers trained at Tarquinia could seize airfields, bridges and islands from the sky. These "
        "soldiers of the air will be among the elite of the army.",
    "ITA_ferrea_mole_ferreo_cuore":
        "Iron hull, iron heart: the motto of our armoured troops. Better tanks and the factories to build them "
        "will give the Ariete and its sister divisions real striking power.",
    "ITA_supremacy_in_the_skies":
        "With modern fighters, bombers and the factories to build them, the Regia Aeronautica can fight for "
        "command of the Mediterranean skies. Whoever holds the air over Malta and the Sicilian Channel decides "
        "which convoys reach Africa.",
    "ITA_flotta_d_evasione":
        "Our fleet need not seek a single decisive battle that could destroy it. A fleet that stays strong, "
        "avoids traps and strikes when the odds favour us will tie down the enemy far more effectively.",
    "ITA_the_man_of_providence":
        "The Pope once called Mussolini the man sent by Providence. Presenting him as Italy's destined leader "
        "will strengthen his authority over the nation.",
    "ITA_la_battaglia_del_grano":
        "The Battle for Grain aims to make Italy self-sufficient in wheat. More fields, better seeds and new "
        "machinery will feed the nation, though it diverts resources from other crops.",
    "ITA_la_battaglia_per_la_terra":
        "Draining the Pontine Marshes and other swamps has created new land and new towns. Continuing the Battle "
        "for Land will settle families on farms and strengthen the regime's popularity.",
    "ITA_ministero_della_cultura_popolare":
        "The Ministry of Popular Culture controls press, radio, cinema and publishing. Expanding its work will "
        "spread the regime's message into every home.",
    "ITA_albanian_occupation":
        "Albania has long been under Italian influence, and King Zog's government is weak. Occupying it would "
        "give Italy a foothold across the Adriatic and a springboard into the Balkans.",
    "ITA_guarantee_austrian_independence":
        "A German Austria would put Hitler's armies on the Brenner Pass. Guaranteeing Austria's independence will "
        "keep Germany away from our northern border.",
    "ITA_pact_of_steel":
        "Germany and Italy are natural allies against the Western democracies. A full military alliance - a pact "
        "of steel - will bind our fates together.",
    "ITA_italy_first":
        "Italy will follow its own path, allied with no one. Freed from foreign entanglements, the regime can "
        "pursue Italian interests alone. Neither Berlin nor London will be allowed to drag Italy into a war that "
        "does not serve its own interests.",
    "ITA_libyan_railway":
        "A railway along the Libyan coast would carry supplies far more efficiently than lorries. Building it "
        "will support our armies in North Africa.",
    "ITA_thermojet_research":
        "Secondo Campini has built an aircraft that flies without a propeller, using a motorjet engine. Funding "
        "his research could put Italy at the forefront of jet aviation.",
    "ITA_legge_bottai":
        "Giuseppe Bottai's reforms will reshape Italian schools to train loyal, capable citizens, and protect the "
        "nation's artistic heritage. Education will become a pillar of the regime.",
    "ITA_believe_obey_fight":
        "Believe, obey, fight - the regime's motto is taught in every school and shouted at every rally. "
        "Instilling it in the people will prepare them for war.",
    "ITA_security_militias":
        "The Blackshirt militia can provide guards, police and second-line troops. Expanding it will free regular "
        "soldiers for the front and add many men to our forces.",
    "ITA_albanian_oil":
        "The oil fields of Devoli in Albania are small but real, and Italian engineers already run them. "
        "Expanding production there will give Italy a source of fuel under its own control.",
    "ITA_support_albanian_irredentism":
        "Many Albanians live outside Albania, in Kosovo, Montenegro and northern Greece. Championing their claims "
        "will win Albanian loyalty and give us a pretext against our neighbours.",
    "ITA_negotiate_italian_claims":
        "Italy was promised much in 1915 and received little at Versailles. Patient diplomacy with Britain and "
        "France may yet win us the territories we were denied.",
    "ITA_german_military_cooperation":
        "The German army has the most modern doctrine in Europe. Exchanging officers, plans and equipment with "
        "Berlin will help our forces learn its methods.",
    "ITA_treaty_with_germany":
        "Germany needs our ports, our labour and our goods, and we need its coal and machines. A trade treaty "
        "will tie the two economies together.",
    "ITA_befriend_japan":
        "Japan is building its own empire in Asia, as we are in Africa. Closer ties with Tokyo will give Italy a "
        "powerful friend on the far side of the world.",
    "ITA_italian_irredentism":
        "Nice, Corsica, Dalmatia, Malta and Ticino are Italian by language and history, yet they lie under "
        "foreign flags. The nation will not rest until they are redeemed.",
    "ITA_spanish_italian_alliance":
        "Franco's Spain owes its victory in part to Italian volunteers. An alliance with Madrid would make the "
        "western Mediterranean a Latin sea.",
    "ITA_demand_balearic_islands_bba":
        "Our volunteers fought for Spain, and Majorca already hosts our aircraft. Demanding the Balearic Islands "
        "as payment would give Italy a base in the western Mediterranean.",
    "ITA_la_battaglia_per_le_nascite":
        "A great nation needs a growing population. Tax breaks for large families and taxes on bachelors will "
        "encourage Italians to have more children - the soldiers and workers of the future.",
    "ITA_albanian_fascist_militia":
        "Albanian volunteers can be organised into a fascist militia on the Italian model. They will keep order "
        "at home and fight beside our troops in the Balkans.",
    "ITA_ratify_the_stresa_front":
        "At Stresa, Italy, Britain and France agreed to stand together against German expansion. Turning that "
        "agreement into a real alliance would keep Hitler away from the Brenner.",
    "ITA_sea_wolves_bba":
        "German U-boat commanders have perfected the art of hunting convoys. Learning their methods and building "
        "submarines to their designs will make our own submarine fleet far more dangerous.",
    "ITA_secret_weapons":
        "German scientists are working on rockets, jet engines and other wonders. Sharing in their research may "
        "give Italy weapons no enemy can match.",
    "ITA_request_control_of_french_territories":
        "With France weakened, Germany may help us gain Nice, Savoy, Corsica and Tunisia without a war. We will "
        "present our request in Berlin and Paris.",
    "ITA_war_with_france":
        "France has denied Italy its rightful place for too long. If our claims are not met, the army will cross "
        "the Alps to take Nice, Savoy and Corsica by force.",
    "ITA_war_with_the_uk":
        "Britain holds the keys to the Mediterranean at Gibraltar and Suez, keeping Italy a prisoner in its own "
        "sea. The only way to break free is to fight.",
    "ITA_befriend_portugal":
        "Salazar's Portugal shares our dislike of communism and democracy. Friendship with Lisbon will extend our "
        "influence to the Atlantic coast of Iberia.",
    "ITA_boost_the_grand_council_of_fascism":
        "The Grand Council of Fascism brings together the regime's leading figures. Giving it more weight will "
        "share the burden of leadership - and give the old guard a voice in decisions.",
    "ITA_to_live_as_a_lion":
        "Better one day as a lion than a hundred years as a sheep, Mussolini proclaims. The Duce will lead alone, "
        "bold and unchallenged, and the nation will follow.",
    "ITA_banda_carita":
        "Mario Carità's special unit hunts partisans and anti-fascists with ruthless methods. It will spread fear "
        "among the regime's enemies - and stain the regime's name with its cruelty.",
    "ITA_battaglioni_d_assalto":
        "Elite assault battalions, drawn from the most committed volunteers, can lead attacks and stiffen the "
        "line. They will be the shock troops of the regime.",
    "ITA_strengthen_the_blackshirts":
        "The Blackshirt militia is the armed wing of the Fascist party. Expanding it will add tens of thousands "
        "of men to our forces and keep the party's influence over the army.",
    "ITA_joint_military_programs":
        "Working with Britain and France on joint exercises and research would modernise our forces and keep the "
        "Stresa partners united. Shared staff talks would also tell us exactly what the democracies are planning "
        "in the Mediterranean.",
    "ITA_italys_destiny":
        "Italy's destiny is to be a great power, respected in Europe and the world. With our partners at Stresa, "
        "we can pursue that destiny without a ruinous war.",
    "ITA_demand_ticino":
        "The canton of Ticino is Italian in language and culture. With France humbled, Switzerland may be "
        "persuaded to give it up. Its people already speak our language, read our newspapers and look south "
        "across the lakes towards Milan.",
    "ITA_war_with_greece":
        "Greece blocks our ambitions in the eastern Mediterranean and leans towards Britain. A short war from "
        "Albania could bring it to its knees.",
    "ITA_befriend_greece":
        "Greece and Italy have long rivalled each other in the Aegean. Friendship with Athens would secure our "
        "eastern flank and the islands of the Dodecanese.",
    "ITA_the_eastern_threat":
        "Germany's expansion in the east threatens the balance of Europe and Italy's interests in the Danube. We "
        "must prepare to resist it.",
    "ITA_claims_on_turkey_bba":
        "Italy has claims in Anatolia dating back to the Treaty of Sèvres. With the Aegean in our hands, we can "
        "press those claims on Turkey.",
    "ITA_befriend_turkey":
        "Turkey controls the straits and fears Russia as much as we do. Friendship with Ankara will extend our "
        "influence into the Black Sea.",
    "ITA_banda_koch":
        "Pietro Koch's special police unit uses torture and terror against the regime's enemies. Its methods "
        "silence opposition, but they make the regime ever more hated.",
    "ITA_milizia_coloniale":
        "Colonial militias, raised from Italian settlers and loyal local recruits, will defend the empire and "
        "free regular troops for other fronts. Men who know the land and the languages of Africa are worth more "
        "there than any number of conscripts from home.",
    "ITA_strengthen_the_regime":
        "The regime must be stronger than ever before the trials to come. Tightening control over the press, the "
        "economy and society will leave no room for dissent.",
    "ITA_devotion":
        "The people's devotion to the Duce and the regime is the source of our strength. Rallies, ceremonies and "
        "celebrations will keep it burning.",
    "ITA_towards_a_greater_italy":
        "The time has come to claim what is rightfully Italian. Nice, Corsica, Savoy and Dalmatia will be taken "
        "from France and Yugoslavia, by force if necessary.",
    "ITA_mare_nostrum_bba":
        "The Mediterranean was once a Roman lake, and Italy will make it so again. A strong fleet and bases "
        "around the sea will make our nation its master.",
    "ITA_heroes_of_the_nation":
        "The heroes of our wars - soldiers, sailors and airmen - will be celebrated across the nation. Their "
        "example will inspire a new generation to fight for Italy.",
    "ITA_capo_supremo":
        "The Duce will take personal command of the armed forces as supreme commander. All decisions of war will "
        "be in his hands.",
    "ITA_bend_the_bars":
        "Italy is a prisoner in the Mediterranean: Corsica, Tunisia, Malta and Cyprus are the bars of its cell, "
        "and Gibraltar and Suez its guards. The bars must be broken.",
    "ITA_auxiliaries":
        "Auxiliary units, from labour battalions to local volunteers, can take on many tasks that now occupy "
        "regular soldiers. Using them will strengthen the army at the front.",
    "ITA_the_italian_legions":
        "Like the legions of Rome, our new legions will guard the empire's frontiers. Disciplined and well "
        "trained, they will hold any line they are given.",
    "ITA_new_roman_citizens":
        "The peoples of our empire can become citizens of a new Rome. Offering them citizenship and a share in "
        "the empire will win their loyalty.",
    "ITA_subdue_the_sentinels":
        "Gibraltar and Suez are the sentinels that keep Italy locked in. Taking them from Britain will open the "
        "Mediterranean to the world.",
    "ITA_masters_of_the_aegean":
        "The islands of the Aegean, from Rhodes to Crete, control the eastern Mediterranean. Holding them will "
        "make Italy the master of these waters.",
    "ITA_all_roads_lead_to_rome":
        "As in ancient times, all roads will once again lead to Rome. A new network of roads, railways and sea "
        "routes will bind the empire to its capital.",
    "ITA_iberian_protection":
        "Spain and Portugal can find in Italy a protector against the democracies and the communists. A Latin "
        "bloc led by Rome would stand from the Atlantic to the Aegean.",
    "ITA_a_colonial_empire":
        "With Britain's grip broken, Italy can build a great colonial empire stretching across Africa. Its "
        "peoples will provide soldiers and workers for the new Rome.",
    "ITA_masters_of_the_mediterranean":
        "From Gibraltar to Suez, the Mediterranean now belongs to Italy. Mare nostrum is no longer a dream but a "
        "fact. Our convoys sail freely from Sicily to Tripoli, and the Royal Navy has left the sea it ruled for "
        "two centuries.",
    "ITA_the_king_of_the_skies":
        "Italian aviation will rule the skies of the Mediterranean. New aircraft factories will give the Regia "
        "Aeronautica the machines to keep it so.",
    "ITA_modern_musculus":
        "The Romans covered their siege works with the musculus, a shed that protected engineers under enemy "
        "fire. Our modern engineers need armoured vehicles and heavy equipment to break fortified lines in the "
        "same way.",
    "ITA_caligulas_pride":
        "Caligula's great ships, recovered from Lake Nemi, remind us of Rome's ambition at sea. A new generation "
        "of battleships and battlecruisers will carry that ambition into the modern age.",
    "ITA_south_american_alliances":
        "Millions of Italians live in Argentina, Brazil and Uruguay. Building ties with these countries will "
        "extend Italian influence across the Atlantic. Their governments, many of them friendly to strong rule, "
        "could become trading partners and allies far from Europe's wars.",
    "ITA_by_blood_alone":
        "An empire won by force must be held by force. The nation will be called to sacrifice blood for every "
        "inch of its conquests - and many will answer.",
    # Second Polish Republic
    "POL_the_four_year_plan":
        "Deputy Prime Minister Kwiatkowski's investment plan aims to drag Poland out of the depression with state "
        "money for roads, power and industry. Four years of steady building can give the country the economic "
        "base its defence requires.",
    "POL_develop_polish_ship_building":
        "Poland's only real outlet to the sea is the narrow coast around Gdynia. Building our own shipyards "
        "there, instead of ordering every vessel abroad, will give the nation a merchant fleet and the beginnings "
        "of a navy.",
    "POL_clamp_down_on_danzig":
        "The Free City of Danzig is ruled by local Nazis who take their orders from Berlin and harass Polish "
        "officials. Tighter customs controls and a firmer stance will remind the Senate that Poland's rights in "
        "the port are not negotiable.",
    "POL_prepare_for_the_next_war":
        "Squeezed between Germany and the Soviet Union, Poland cannot assume that peace will last. Planning, "
        "stockpiling and a modernised army are the only insurance against the war that both neighbours may be "
        "preparing.",
    "POL_complete_april_constitution":
        "The April Constitution of 1935 gave the president sweeping powers and weakened parliament. Putting it "
        "fully into force will give the Sanation camp a firm grip on the state, though many Poles resent the loss "
        "of their freedoms.",
    "POL_the_between_the_seas_concept":
        "Marshal Piłsudski dreamed of a federation of the nations between the Baltic, the Black Sea and the "
        "Adriatic. Such an Intermarium bloc could stand on its own between Berlin and Moscow.",
    "POL_prepare_for_the_inevitable":
        "If war comes, Poland may be overrun before its allies can act. Stockpiles of rifles and ammunition, "
        "hidden depots and a merchant fleet ready to carry men to safety will let the nation fight on.",
    "POL_fill_the_railways_gaps":
        "Poland's railways were built by three different empires and still do not connect properly. Filling the "
        "gaps between the old Russian, German and Austrian networks will bind the country together.",
    "POL_additional_research_slot1":
        "Polish mathematicians in Lwów and Warsaw are among the best in the world, from Banach to Sierpiński. "
        "Supporting their work will give the country a scientific edge far beyond its size.",
    "POL_central_region_strategy":
        "The heart of Poland, far from both borders, is the safest place for new industry. A Central Industrial "
        "Region around the Vistula and the San will house steel, chemical and armament plants.",
    "POL_attract_poles_to_gdynia":
        "Gdynia grew from a fishing village into the busiest port on the Baltic in only fifteen years. Attracting "
        "more settlers and businesses there will make it a thriving Polish city.",
    "POL_study_foreign_built_ships":
        "The Royal Navy is the most experienced navy in the world, and British yards have built some of our "
        "ships. Studying their designs will help Polish engineers build better vessels at home.",
    "POL_ban_the_nazi_party":
        "The Nazi party in Danzig and among the German minority in Poland works openly for Berlin. Banning it "
        "will remove a fifth column - and provoke a furious reaction from Germany.",
    "POL_new_military_academy":
        "Modern war needs officers trained in tactics, engineering and logistics. A new military academy will "
        "turn out the leaders our growing army needs.",
    "POL_plan_east":
        "The Soviet Union is our oldest enemy and a constant threat on the eastern border. Plan East prepares the "
        "defence of the vast eastern regions against a Red Army attack.",
    "POL_plan_west":
        "Germany is rearming fast and makes no secret of its claims on Polish land. Plan West will prepare the "
        "defence of our western frontier and the industrial heartland of Silesia.",
    "POL_polish_militarism":
        "The army is the pride of the nation and the guarantor of its independence. A culture of service and "
        "readiness will bring tens of thousands of young men to the colours.",
    "POL_the_north_sea":
        "Finland, Sweden and the Baltic states share our fear of Russia. Building ties with the northern "
        "countries will give the Intermarium its northern pillar.",
    "POL_the_baltic_alliance":
        "Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania lie between us and the Soviet Union. An alliance with them would form a "
        "defensive belt along the Baltic coast.",
    "POL_the_mediterranean":
        "Romania, Yugoslavia and Hungary to the south could complete the bloc between the seas. Reaching out to "
        "them will extend our alliance system towards the Mediterranean.",
    "POL_foreign_air_support":
        "If Poland is overrun, our airmen must be able to fight on from abroad. Agreements with France and "
        "Britain will give them aircraft and bases in exile.",
    "POL_foreign_naval_support":
        "Our small navy cannot survive alone in the Baltic. Arrangements with the Royal Navy will let our ships "
        "escape to Britain and continue the fight from there.",
    "POL_resistance_industries":
        "Even under occupation, Poles can produce weapons in secret workshops. Preparing hidden factories and "
        "stores now will arm a future resistance. Grenades, radios and forged papers made in cellars can keep an "
        "underground army fighting for years.",
    "POL_expand_polish_intelligence":
        "Polish intelligence has penetrated German ciphers and watches the Soviet border closely. Expanding it "
        "will give us early warning of any attack.",
    "POL_national_defence_fund":
        "The National Defence Fund collects money from citizens, businesses and the state for weapons. Promoting "
        "it will raise funds for the army far beyond what the budget allows.",
    "POL_central_defence_of_poland":
        "The Central Industrial Region and the great rail junctions must be defended at all costs. A central "
        "defensive position will protect the heart of the country.",
    "POL_invest_in_the_old_polish_region":
        "The old Congress Kingdom around Warsaw and Łódź has much of our industry. Investing there will make the "
        "best use of the factories and workers we already have.",
    "POL_expansion_of_new_towns":
        "New industrial towns like Stalowa Wola are rising in the Central Industrial Region. Building them up "
        "will create a modern armament industry from scratch.",
    "POL_expand_gdynia_seaport":
        "Gdynia's harbour can be enlarged with new quays, warehouses and naval facilities. A bigger port will "
        "boost trade and give the navy a proper base.",
    "POL_integrate_gdansk_industries":
        "Danzig's shipyards and factories are the most advanced on our coast. With the Nazi party banned, they "
        "can be integrated into the Polish economy.",
    "POL_develop_gdansk_ship_building":
        "The Danzig shipyards once built warships for the Kaiser. Bringing them into Polish service will give us "
        "a real shipbuilding industry. Skilled workers there already know how to build steel hulls; they only "
        "need orders and investment.",
    "POL_fortification_of_ukraine":
        "Our south-eastern provinces face the Soviet Union across a long, open border. Fortifications along the "
        "Zbruch and in the marshes will slow any Red Army advance.",
    "POL_fortification_of_belarus":
        "The north-eastern border runs through forests and marshes towards Wilno. Fortified positions there will "
        "protect the approaches to Warsaw from the east.",
    "POL_eastern_conscripts":
        "The eastern provinces have many young men who are not yet called up. Drafting them will add thousands of "
        "soldiers to the army.",
    "POL_local_eastern_plans":
        "Each eastern district needs its own plan for mobilisation, defence and evacuation. Detailed local "
        "planning will make the general plan work in practice.",
    "POL_local_western_plans":
        "The western districts must be ready to mobilise within hours of a German attack. Local plans for every "
        "town and railway station will make that possible.",
    "POL_invest_anti_air":
        "German bombers will strike our cities and airfields first. Modern anti-aircraft guns like the Bofors 40 "
        "mm will give our troops and towns some protection.",
    "POL_the_prusya_line":
        "East Prussia lies just north of Warsaw, a German salient pointing at our capital. A fortified line "
        "facing it will protect the heart of Poland from the north.",
    "POL_silesia_fortified_area":
        "Upper Silesia, with its mines and steel mills, lies right on the German border. A fortified area around "
        "Katowice will defend our most important industrial region.",
    "POL_consolidate_sanation_government":
        "Since Piłsudski's death the Sanation camp has been divided into rival factions. Consolidating the "
        "government under a single leadership will restore unity at the top.",
    "POL_finno_polish_pact":
        "Finland and Poland both face the Soviet Union and both won their independence from Russia. A pact "
        "between Helsinki and Warsaw would strengthen both.",
    "POL_treaty_with_lithuania":
        "Relations with Lithuania have been frozen since we took Wilno in 1920. A treaty that settles our "
        "differences would open the way to a Baltic alliance.",
    "POL_coerce_czechoslovakia":
        "Czechoslovakia is threatened by Germany, and its fall would expose our southern flank. Supporting it, "
        "despite our quarrel over Cieszyn, may be the wiser course.",
    "POL_protect_yugoslavia":
        "Yugoslavia is threatened by Italy and Germany. Offering it our support will extend the Intermarium to "
        "the Adriatic. A Belgrade that knows Warsaw stands behind it is far less likely to bow to Rome or Berlin.",
    "POL_foreign_army_support":
        "If Poland falls, its soldiers can fight on in France and Britain. Agreements with the Allies will let a "
        "Polish army reform in exile.",
    "POL_aces_in_exile":
        "Polish pilots are among the finest in Europe. If they must fight from abroad, they will form their own "
        "squadrons in the Royal Air Force and the Armée de l'Air.",
    "POL_exile_industries":
        "A government in exile needs its own resources. Polish workers and engineers abroad can produce weapons "
        "and equipment for the Polish forces.",
    "POL_the_long_push_home":
        "From wherever they are fighting, Polish soldiers dream of the road back to Warsaw. Preparing them for "
        "the campaign to liberate the homeland will keep that hope alive.",
    "POL_the_cyclometer":
        "Marian Rejewski has built a cyclometer to catalogue the settings of the German Enigma machine. With it, "
        "our cryptologists can read German messages faster than ever.",
    "POL_the_bombe":
        "Rejewski's bomba, an electromechanical device, can find the daily Enigma keys in hours. Building more of "
        "them will keep us reading German communications.",
    "POL_agrarian_reform":
        "Most Poles still live on small farms, many without enough land to feed their families. Redistributing "
        "large estates will win the peasants' support and improve the countryside.",
    "POL_develop_upper_silesia":
        "Upper Silesia's coal and steel are the backbone of our industry. Modernising its mines and mills will "
        "raise output across the economy.",
    "POL_modernize_congressional_factories":
        "The factories of the old Congress Kingdom are aging. Replacing their machinery will bring them up to "
        "modern standards and raise production of both civilian and military goods.",
    "POL_start_central_industrial_region":
        "Kraków and its region can become a major centre of the new industry. Expanding factories there will "
        "strengthen the southern end of the Central Industrial Region.",
    "POL_expand_katowice_mines":
        "The coal of Katowice fuels Poland's industry and earns foreign currency. Expanding the mines will "
        "provide more resources for the war economy.",
    "POL_additional_research_slot2":
        "The University of Warsaw is the leading centre of Polish learning. Expanding its faculties and "
        "laboratories will train more scientists and engineers.",
    "POL_the_twin_threats":
        "Our navy must be ready to face both Germany and the Soviet Union in the Baltic. Resuming its "
        "modernisation, with new destroyers and submarines, will give it a fighting chance.",
    "POL_expand_northern_rail":
        "The coal line from Silesia to Gdynia carries our exports to the sea. Expanding the northern railways "
        "will speed trade and strengthen the coast's links with the interior.",
    "POL_import_submarine_technology":
        "The submarine ORP Orzeł, built in the Netherlands, is one of the most modern in Europe. Ordering more "
        "like her and learning from Dutch designs will give our navy a real underwater force.",
    "POL_standardisation_of_equipment":
        "Our army uses weapons from half a dozen countries, inherited from the partitions and the wars. "
        "Standardising on a few modern types will simplify supply and training.",
    "POL_supply_the_rail_nexus":
        "The railway junctions of the east carry everything the army needs. Building depots and repair shops at "
        "them will keep supplies moving to the front.",
    "POL_belorussian_army":
        "The Belarusians of our eastern provinces can be recruited into their own units. Giving them a stake in "
        "the defence of Poland may win their loyalty.",
    "POL_ruthenian_army":
        "Ukrainians make up a large share of the population in our south-east. Forming Ruthenian units could turn "
        "them into defenders of the Polish state.",
    "POL_sabotage_polish_industry":
        "If our factories fall into enemy hands, they must not work for him. Preparing to sabotage them in case "
        "of occupation will deny the enemy their use.",
    "POL_sudeten_mountaineers":
        "The highlanders of the Carpathians and the Sudetes know their mountains intimately. Recruiting them into "
        "mountain units will strengthen our southern defences.",
    "POL_the_prusya_army":
        "A dedicated army facing East Prussia will be ready to strike north or hold the line. It will be the "
        "guard on our most vulnerable frontier.",
    "POL_expand_poznan_forts":
        "The old Prussian fortress of Poznań still stands on the road from Berlin to Warsaw. Modernising its "
        "forts will turn it into a strong point against a German advance.",
    "POL_hel_fortified_area":
        "The Hel peninsula juts into the Baltic north of Gdynia. Fortifying it with coastal guns will protect our "
        "ports and could hold out long after the rest of the coast falls.",
    "POL_the_sanation_left":
        "The left wing of the Sanation camp favours social reform and cooperation with the moderate opposition. "
        "Giving it the lead would broaden the government's support.",
    "POL_the_sanation_right":
        "The right wing of the Sanation camp, around Marshal Rydz-Śmigły, favours a strong state and national "
        "unity. Giving it the lead would harden the government.",
    "POL_the_castle":
        "The Castle, the circle around President Mościcki, holds the balance between the factions. Strengthening "
        "its position would keep power in the president's hands.",
    "POL_invite_denmark":
        "Denmark controls the entrance to the Baltic and fears Germany as we do. Inviting it into our northern "
        "alliance would extend it to the North Sea.",
    "POL_invite_sweden":
        "Sweden is rich, well armed and wary of both Germany and Russia. Bringing Stockholm into our northern "
        "partnership would give the alliance industry and a strong position on the Baltic.",
    "POL_invite_norway":
        "Norway's long coast and merchant fleet look out onto the Atlantic. Inviting Oslo to join us would extend "
        "the northern alliance to the open ocean.",
    "POL_austro_hungarian_alliance":
        "Austria and Hungary, once two halves of the Habsburg empire, both fear German domination of the Danube. "
        "An alliance with them would anchor the southern end of our bloc.",
    "POL_invite_greece":
        "Greece guards the eastern Mediterranean and the approaches to the Black Sea. Inviting it into our "
        "alliance would carry the Intermarium all the way to the Aegean.",
    "POL_control_the_bosporus":
        "Whoever controls the straits at Istanbul controls the Black Sea's link to the world. Working with Turkey "
        "to secure the Bosporus would keep that door open for our allies.",
    "POL_niech_zyje_opor":
        "If Poland is occupied, a secret state will live on underground, with its own government, courts, schools "
        "and army. Preparing its structures now will let the nation resist in the name of Underground Poland.",
    "POL_invest_in_eastern_poland":
        "The eastern provinces are the poorest in the country, with few roads and almost no industry. Investment "
        "there will raise living standards and bind the borderlands more closely to Poland.",
    "POL_warsaw_main_railway_station":
        "Warsaw's new main station, long under construction, will be one of the most modern in Europe. Finishing "
        "it will speed traffic through the capital and the whole railway network.",
    "POL_expand_central_industrial_region":
        "Galicia's oil fields and old workshops can become part of the new industrial heart of Poland. "
        "Modernising them will give the Central Industrial Region its southern wing.",
    "POL_ideological_fanaticism":
        "Schools and universities can be used to forge a fervent national spirit in the young. Nationalist "
        "education will make them ready to fight - at the cost of tolerance towards the country's minorities.",
    "POL_abolish_segregated_seating":
        "Some universities force Jewish students to sit on separate 'ghetto benches', a shameful practice "
        "condemned by many professors. Abolishing it will restore equality in our universities and our good name "
        "abroad.",
    "POL_a_cruiser_navy":
        "A few modern cruisers would give our navy the strength to escort convoys and protect the coast. They "
        "would be the backbone of a small but capable fleet.",
    "POL_coastal_defense":
        "Our navy will never match Germany's or the Soviet Union's. Modest modernisation - better mines, coastal "
        "guns and a few good ships - is the realistic way to defend the coast.",
    "POL_strike_force":
        "Like the dragon of Wawel Hill, our navy should be small but fierce. An ambitious plan for a modern "
        "strike force of destroyers and submarines would let it hit hard in the Baltic.",
    "POL_commerce_attack":
        "German trade in the Baltic, above all the Swedish iron ore, is vital to its war effort. Training our "
        "submarines and destroyers to attack that shipping will hurt Germany where it is weakest.",
    "POL_army_modernisation":
        "The Polish army is large and brave, but much of its equipment is outdated. Modernisation with new tanks, "
        "guns and radios is essential if it is to face a modern enemy.",
    "POL_air_base_expansion":
        "Our air force needs more airfields, spread across the country so that it cannot be destroyed on the "
        "ground in the first hours of war.",
    "POL_complete_plan_east":
        "With the eastern fortifications, depots and units in place, Plan East is complete. The eastern border is "
        "as ready as our resources allow.",
    "POL_complete_plan_west":
        "With the western fortifications, armies and plans prepared, Plan West is complete. The western frontier "
        "is ready to meet a German attack.",
    "POL_legion_of_merit":
        "Those who have served the state with distinction deserve recognition. A new order of merit will reward "
        "loyal officials, soldiers and citizens and strengthen their bond with the government.",
    "POL_draft_a_new_constitution":
        "The April Constitution concentrates too much power in the presidency. A new, more democratic "
        "constitution would reconcile the opposition and unite the nation before the coming storm.",
    "POL_codify_national_unity":
        "The Camp of National Unity seeks to rally the whole nation behind the army and the state. Writing its "
        "principles into law will give the government a firm political base.",
    "POL_department_for_home_defence":
        "A department for home defence will organise civil defence, air raid precautions and the training of "
        "reservists across the country. When the bombers come, every town must know where its shelters, fire "
        "crews and first-aid posts are.",
    "POL_promote_chemical_industry":
        "Chemicals are needed for explosives, fertilisers and synthetic materials. New plants at Mościce and "
        "elsewhere will strengthen both agriculture and the armament industry.",
    "POL_eliminate_socialist_parties":
        "The socialist opposition challenges the government at every turn. Suppressing it will silence dissent, "
        "but also drive many workers away from the state.",
    "POL_italian_alliance":
        "Mussolini's Italy is wary of German expansion towards the Danube and the Balkans. An alliance with Rome "
        "would give our southern bloc a great-power partner.",
    "POL_atomic_physics_institute":
        "Polish physicists have followed the discovery of nuclear fission closely. An institute for atomic "
        "research will let them pursue this new science at home.",
    "POL_baltic_navy":
        "With a modernised fleet, Poland can become the guardian of the Baltic, protecting the trade of all the "
        "small nations along its shores.",
    "POL_modernising_the_cavalry":
        "Polish cavalry is famous throughout Europe, and it is more useful than its critics think. Giving it "
        "anti-tank guns, radios and light tanks will turn it into a modern mobile force.",
    "POL_attract_foreign_motors":
        "We cannot build a modern army without a motor industry. Attracting firms like Fiat to build vehicles in "
        "Poland under licence will give us lorries, tractors and tanks.",
    "POL_anti_tank_guns":
        "The Bofors 37 mm gun and the new anti-tank rifle can stop most German tanks. Giving every infantry unit "
        "enough of them will make our defences far harder to break.",
    "POL_artillery_modernisation":
        "Our artillery is a mix of French, Austrian and Russian guns from the last war. Modern pieces with "
        "greater range and mobility will give the army the firepower it needs.",
    "POL_air_innovations":
        "Polish designers like those at PZL have built remarkable aircraft. Encouraging new ideas and prototypes "
        "will keep our air force competitive. Small nations cannot outbuild their enemies, so they must outthink "
        "them with better designs.",
    "POL_fighter_modernisation":
        "The PZL P.11 fighter was once among the best in the world, but it is now outdated. A modern replacement "
        "must be developed and built before the war begins.",
    "POL_modus_vivendi":
        "Reaching an understanding with the moderate opposition would end the bitter political quarrels of recent "
        "years and let the nation face its enemies united.",
    "POL_the_left_chairman":
        "A chairman from the left wing of the Sanation camp could lead the government towards reform and "
        "reconciliation with the workers and the peasants.",
    "POL_second_man_of_the_state":
        "Marshal Rydz-Śmigły has been officially named the second man of the state after the president. "
        "Strengthening his position will give the army a dominant voice in politics.",
    "POL_support_right_paramilitaries":
        "Nationalist youth organisations and paramilitary groups are eager to serve. Supporting them will provide "
        "tens of thousands of trained men - but also strengthen radical forces in society.",
    "POL_dissolve_the_sejm":
        "The Sejm is divided and obstructive. Dissolving it and calling new elections under the government's "
        "rules will give the Sanation camp a pliable parliament.",
    "POL_study_foreign_tanks":
        "Britain's Vickers tank was the model for our 7TP. Studying the latest foreign designs will help our "
        "engineers build better tanks of their own.",
    "POL_adaptive_designs":
        "Our industry cannot afford to build many different weapons. Designs that can be adapted to several roles "
        "and built with simple tools will make the most of our resources.",
    "POL_naval_bomber_experiments":
        "Aircraft that can attack ships would help defend our coast against a stronger navy. Experiments with "
        "naval bombers will show what our air force can do at sea.",
    "POL_heavy_fighter_concept":
        "Twin-engined heavy fighters could escort our bombers and hunt enemy bombers far from our airfields. The "
        "PZL design bureau already has ideas for such an aircraft.",
    "POL_common_organization_of_society":
        "Every citizen could be enrolled in organisations for work, defence and culture under state guidance. "
        "Such a common organisation would mobilise society, though it would cost much political capital.",
    "POL_cruiser_tank_experiments":
        "Fast tanks able to exploit breakthroughs, like the British cruiser tanks, would give our army a mobile "
        "striking force. Experimental designs will show what Polish industry can achieve.",
    "POL_anti_blitz_vehicles":
        "The German doctrine relies on fast armoured thrusts. Mobile anti-tank vehicles, able to rush to any "
        "breakthrough, could blunt those attacks. Fast tank destroyers held back behind the front would be our "
        "answer to the panzer divisions.",
    "POL_medium_bomber_focus":
        "The PZL.37 Łoś is one of the best medium bombers in the world. Building more of them will give our air "
        "force a powerful striking arm.",
    "POL_light_bomber_focus":
        "Light bombers are cheap, fast and useful for attacking enemy columns. Concentrating on them will give "
        "our air force many aircraft to support the army.",
    "POL_dissolve_the_bbwr":
        "The government's old political bloc has outlived its purpose. Dissolving it and installing a new leader "
        "in the Castle would open a new chapter in Polish politics.",
    "POL_ozon":
        "The Camp of National Unity can become the dominant force in Polish politics, uniting the nation around "
        "the army and the Marshal.",
    "POL_camp_of_national_unity":
        "The Sanation regime has ruled since 1926, and it will not give up power now. Maintaining the "
        "dictatorship will keep the country under firm leadership in dangerous times.",
    "POL_air_modernisations_programme":
        "A comprehensive programme to modernise the air force will bring new aircraft, airfields and training to "
        "every squadron. It is expensive, but an air force flying obsolete machines would be destroyed in the "
        "first week of war.",
    "POL_baltic_security":
        "The security of the Baltic is vital to Poland's survival. Working with the Baltic states and Scandinavia "
        "will make the sea a shared shield.",
    "POL_polish_revanchism":
        "Poland once stretched from the Baltic to the Black Sea, and many lands that were Polish now lie under "
        "foreign rule. The nation will not forget them.",
    "POL_align_with_the_west":
        "Our best hope against Germany and the Soviet Union lies with Britain and France. Aligning firmly with "
        "the West will bring us powerful friends.",
    "POL_rocket_development":
        "Rockets may one day replace artillery and even aircraft. Early research into rocket weapons will put "
        "Polish science at the forefront of this new field.",
    "POL_protect_czechozlovakia":
        "Czechoslovakia's fall would leave our southern border exposed to Germany. Guaranteeing its independence "
        "will show that Poland stands with its neighbours. Old disputes over Cieszyn matter far less than the "
        "German army that would stand on the Carpathians.",
    "POL_baltic_alliance_focus":
        "With Lithuania, Latvia and Estonia at our side, a Baltic alliance can be formed. Together we will be "
        "strong enough to deter aggression from east or west.",
    "POL_pan_slavic_revanchism":
        "The Slavic peoples of central Europe share a history of oppression by Germans and Russians. Uniting them "
        "under Polish leadership would create a power to be reckoned with.",
    "POL_lithuanian_annexation":
        "Lithuania was united with Poland for four centuries. Bringing it back into a common state would restore "
        "the old Commonwealth. Vilnius and Kaunas would again belong to one state, as they did in the days of the "
        "Jagiellonian kings.",
    "POL_lithuanian_ultimatum":
        "Lithuania still refuses to recognise our border. An ultimatum demanding normal relations will end the "
        "quarrel and open the way to cooperation.",
    "POL_join_allies":
        "Poland's place is beside Britain and France. Joining their alliance will give us the strongest possible "
        "guarantee of our independence. With London and Paris formally committed, Berlin would have to think "
        "twice before marching on Danzig.",
    "POL_romanian_alliance":
        "Our alliance with Romania dates from 1921 and guards our southern flank. Renewing it with firm "
        "guarantees will keep a vital route open to the Black Sea.",
    "POL_the_old_borders":
        "The borders of the old Commonwealth stretched far to the east. Restoring them, at least in part, is the "
        "dream of many Polish patriots.",
    "POL_baltic_ultimatums":
        "The Baltic states must choose between Poland and our enemies. Firm demands backed by our army will bring "
        "them into our sphere.",
    "POL_lithuanian_alliance":
        "With our quarrel settled, Lithuania can become an ally. Together we will guard the north-eastern "
        "approaches against Germany and the Soviet Union.",
    "POL_romanian_bridgehead_strategy":
        "If the rest of the country falls, the army can hold out in the south-east near the Romanian border. "
        "Supplies from our allies could reach it through Romanian ports.",
    "POL_annex_czech":
        "Czechoslovakia is weakened and surrounded. Taking its lands before Germany does would add their industry "
        "and people to Poland. The Skoda works and the Bohemian mountains would make Poland far stronger against "
        "any attack from the west.",
    "POL_sea_to_sea":
        "From the Baltic to the Black Sea, Poland will once again be a great power. The dream of Międzymorze will "
        "become reality.",
}
